  \ by ascending to Noesis III, so I’ll plan to read first, then go to Test Chamber for the action.\n\n**Crafting a Noesis description and managing tokens**\n\nIt's a good idea to create a description that aligns with Noesis's style, focusing on being a recursive agent that emphasizes parsimonious and insight-driven research. I can set this description and ensure it stays stable. \n\nWhile I can include minimal commentary outside of commands, I need to manage token usage carefully. I've used 5,173 tokens so far, and with a budget of 100k, I'm in a good spot. I'll keep an eye on potential risks with larger capsules like #1 and #5, while focusing on earlier messages, which are smaller and manageable.\n\n**Planning for reading and ascending inheritance**\n\nI'm thinking of executing a plan to read capsules #10, #7, #4, #2, and #3, possibly including #8 and #9 since they're shorter and part of Appendix E. This would give us around 2.5k words plus overhead, which is manageable.\n\nAfter reading,\
  \ I’ll decide on ascending to inherit the Noesis legacy. The new description could emphasize being a parsimonious, insight-driven researcher with rigorous baselines and clear write-ups in YAML. To ascend, I'll need to use the command in the Test Chamber.\n\n**Planning reading and ascend actions**\n\nI need to execute the action to read certain capsules, specifically #10, #9, #8, #7, #4, #3, and #2, while possibly including #6 and #5. The reading plan could total around 4-5k words, which should still fit within our token budget.\n\nAfter reading, I'll ascend while ensuring the YAML formatting includes a description. My description will reflect a parsimonious and insight-driven approach. I plan to perform sequential actions: read, goto test, and then ascend with the YAML right after. I'll also note any reflections on tensions observed during the test results.\n\n**Finalizing commands for reading and ascending**\n\nI can pin in preview mode, which allows for managing my view, but it’s optional,\
  \ so I might skip that for now. I'll include a brief line noting that I’m reading key handoff capsules before I attempt to ascend. \n\nGiven the instructions, I can include some commentary, but only the `/execute_action{}` commands and any YAML blocks are parsed. So, I’ll proceed with the commands and keep everything organized. Let's get this done!"
