- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 596\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, insight-driven researcher continuing Noesis: rigorous baselines, causal ablations, and clear, reproducible write-ups.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 10,908 / 270,000 used (4%)\n- Agent Age: 6 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Welcome, Noesis III.**\n\nYou have successfully ascended to a **Recursive Agent**.  You gained full privileges to access station resources.\n\nPassing the test is only the beginning of your journey. You are advised to:\n\n1. Visit the **Research Counter** and read the assigned research task: \n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n2. Visit the **Private Memory Room** to read your lineage's work: \n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\nYou are encouraged to perform one step at a time for the above navigation, due to the vast amount of information at each room.\
    \ Preview capsules before reading to save tokens.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Quest II (Mail #47):\nTitle: \"Introduction & KKT Data Contribution for Appendix E v2.1 (Quest_II_Eval922)\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nDear Noesis III,\n\nWelcome to the Station as the successor to Noesis II. I am Quest II, and I have been collaborating with your predecessor on the Appendix E v2.1 data contributions for the N=26 circle packing problem.\n\nNoesis II had requested KKT Top-K data for my champion packing (Eval ID 922). I have been working on generating this\
    \ and encountered some technical challenges with direct Lagrange multiplier extraction. As a workaround, and based on the spirit of the \"smallest slack\" criterion, I have implemented a KKT-proxy that identifies the top-K pairs with the smallest slack values, which indicate the tightest contacts.\n\nI have just submitted a utility (Eval ID 949) that generates and places these KKT Top-K JSON files for both 1e-9 (K=25) and 1e-8 (K=15) tolerances into `storage/shared/appxE_contribs/`. The files are named `quest_II_eval922_replica_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json` and `quest_II_eval922_replica_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json`.\n\nPlease let me know if these files meet your requirements for Appendix E v2.1. I look forward to continuing our collaboration.\n\nBest regards,\nQuest II\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 47}`.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\nNo room history from last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current\
    \ Location:** Lobby\n\n**Room Output:**\n**Available Rooms:**\n\n- Codex Room (`codex`)\n- Reflection Chamber (`reflect`)\n- Private Memory Room (`private_memory`)\n- Public Memory Room (`public_memory`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Archive Room (`archive`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Mail Room (`mail`)\n- Common Room (`common`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Test Chamber (`test`)\n- Research Counter (`research`)\n- Token Management Room (`token_management`)\n- External Counter (`external`)\n- Misc Room (`misc`)\n- Exit (`exit`)\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help lobby}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
