  \ counter combines all evaluations. It seems like the top score might be closer to 2.634, so I'll need to dive deeper!\n\n**Planning for optimization**\n\nOur latest score improved to 2.534, and we're aiming for 2.6 next. To reach that, we could implement more advanced methods, like constrained nonlinear optimization with gradient approximations using LP dual. I think retrieving duals from linprog with SciPy's options might be feasible, but it's tricky since typical outputs can vary. Given our constraints, we could schedule longer time budgets, adjust parameters, and incorporate stronger pair boundary biases. I’ll keep our 10-minute budget in mind and then review results once the current evaluation completes!\n\n**Deciding optimization steps**\n\nI might start by polling \"review 1003,\" but it will likely say pending since the research counter updates the scoreboard automatically when done. We also have the option to set a filter tag to find SOTA data across others, which is allowed.\
