tick: 634
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noesis/pack/README.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Noesis n=26 — LP-in-the-loop SA+Quench Recipes\n\n  Overview\n  - Objective: maximize sum of radii for 26 circles in unit square.\n  - Inner loop: exact LP (SciPy HiGHS) to compute optimal radii for fixed centers.\n  - Outer loop: stochastic search on centers with:\n    - weighted tight-pair separation,\n    - boundary-inward nudges,\n    - occasional triple neighbor moves,\n    - frequent greedy coordinate quenches,\n    - mild reheating after stagnation.\n  - Multistart seeds: grid + jitters + hex-like + jittered-hex (6 total).\n\n  Best observed\n  - 2.5743 (Eval 1008): 8-min adaptive SA+quench with pair/boundary/triple proposals.\n  - Freeze parameters saved at: storage/noesis/pack/recipe_2_57_freeze.json\n\n  Quick reproduce (compact 8 min; imports lineage module)\n  ```python\n  # run.py\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n  from pack.lp_sa_core\
    \ import run_sa_sizeaware, lp_radii_for_centers\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # 480s budget ~ 8 minutes. pair_exp=1.0 matches 1/(slack+delta) weighting in the freeze.\n      centers, radii, obj = run_sa_sizeaware(budget_s=480.0, pair_exp=1.0)\n      # Final LP tighten\n      r_final, obj_final, ok = lp_radii_for_centers(centers)\n      if ok:\n          radii = r_final\n      return centers, radii\n  ```\n\n  Notes and guidance\n  - Acceptance-ratio target ~0.25–0.35; trials_per_T ~100.\n  - Frequent greedy quenches: after improvements (p≈0.3) and between temperature levels.\n  - Reheating: after ~6 stagnant levels, reheat T and add small jitter to the best.\n  - Budgets >10 min tend to drift; compact 4–8 min runs with good quenches performed better in our tests.\n  - Alternative: 5 min SA warm start + 5 min dual-guided ascent refine (≈2.54 observed).\n\n  Files\n  - recipe_2_57_freeze.json — exact parameter snapshot that produced 2.5743.\n  - lp_sa_core.py — modular SA/dual/utility\
    \ functions used by the recipes.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Preparing README Instructions**


  I think it makes sense to prepare a minimal README in the storage/noesis/pack directory to describe how to use the module. This will be really helpful! But I need to execute the storage actions in the Research Counter while we''re in Private Memory Room. I’ll write instructions in the README file, mentioning reproduction steps and referencing recipe_2_57_freeze.json. It might cost some tokens, but it''s aligned with our plan and beneficial for the future. I''ll also consider storing a script for ease of use.


  **Writing README Content**


  I can definitely instruct how to build run.py to import from storage, similar to before. So, I want to include a few key elements in the README: an overview of the approach and the steps to reproduce the best recipe with a short code snippet.


  I’ll provide a snippet that goes like this: I''ll explain how to import the necessary modules and define the `construct_packing` function using `run_sa_sizeaware`. There’s a lot of detail to clarify about parameters and past adjustments, making sure I don’t mislead anyone about how we arrived at the best run.


  **Creating README Instructions**


  The README will guide how to re-run the best "adaptive SA triple variant" scenario. To save on tokens, I''ll include a code snippet for importing `sa_sizeaware` and setting `pair_exp=1.0`. I want to keep things generic by referring to `recipe_2_57_freeze.json` for weights and clarifying that the pair sampling weight is `1/(slack+1e-9)`.


  I''ll outline the differences between variant scenarios and provide information on targeted budgets and acceptance ratios. It''s important to remind users about token and time budgets as well. I''ll execute the necessary actions to write to the storage.'
