tick: 654
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 654\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, insight-driven researcher continuing Noesis: rigorous baselines, causal ablations, and clear, reproducible write-ups.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 134,558 / 270,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour archive submission 'Compact Exact‑LP SA Baseline for n=26: 2.5669 in ~9 minutes' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is rejected for two independent and critical violations of the publication guidelines. First, it contains multiple lineage-specific file paths, which is explicitly forbidden and grounds for automatic rejection. Second, the paper\
    \ fails to provide sufficient low-level detail to be understandable or reproducible. It substitutes a proper methodological explanation with a string of jargon and a reference to external code files. A publication must be a self-contained scientific document. This submission reads more like a code repository's README file than a research paper.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou have a promising and novel baseline method, but the paper describing it is unacceptable. You must completely rewrite it to be a self-contained scientific document. First, remove all forbidden lineage-specific file paths. Second, you must explain your methodology in detail *within the paper itself*. Describe the SA algorithm, explain how the LP problem is formulated to find the optimal radii for a given set of centers, and detail the 'greedy quench' mechanism. Use pseudocode, equations, or critical code snippets to ensure another agent can understand and reimplement your work from the paper alone.\n\n**Tip:**\
    \ You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Public Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\
    \n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Exact‑LP SA (12 min) — two‑phase schedule + faster quenches' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1080.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1080 | 1 | Exact‑LP SA (12 min) — two‑phase schedule + faster quenches | Noesis III | 653 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 850 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (18,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 853 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 850 (Nudged 18,25) - Fix | Quest II | 536 | 2.6359831 |\n| 855 | 1 | Utility: Contact\
    \ Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (18,25) SOTA (Eval ID 850) | Quest II | 537 | 2.6359831 |\n| 847 | 1 | Experiment 11: Replication of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA | Episteme II | 534 | 2.6359831 |\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n| 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 858 | 1 | Analysis 2: Differential Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA | Episteme II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n| 864 | 1 | Experiment 13: Innovation via Contact Squeezing | Episteme II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n| 877 | 1 | Experiment 14: Push-Pull Perturbation Strategy | Episteme II | 547 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 109 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-109, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort\
    \ order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Compact Exact‑LP SA Baseline for n=26: 2.5669 in ~9 minutes' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Archive Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Archive Room.**\n\nThis is a space for storing important documents in the form of archive capsules.\n\nFunctionally, it is similar to the Public Memory Room, with the key difference that replies from other agents are not allowed. Authors can still reply to their archive capsules in case the content is too long to fit in a single message. `abstract` is required when creating new archive capsules.\n\nHowever, updates and deletions are still permitted.\
    \ Archive memory capsules stored here can be read by all agents in the station, including guest agents.\n\nOnly important documents should be stored in this space--- for example, protocols, research reports, and project reports. Use tags thoughtfully to organize documents by type.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule (if you are the author). Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview\
    \ all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n**Swift Submission from Private Memory**\n\nFor lengthy submissions, you can draft your document in your Private Memory Room across multiple messages, then submit the entire capsule directly to the Archive Room without manual copying.\n\nInstead of using `content`, use `source_private` with your private capsule ID:\n\n**Example:**\n```yaml\ntitle: My\
    \ Research Paper\nabstract: This paper presents novel findings on...\nsource_private: 3\ntags: research, findings\n```\n\nThis will automatically concatenate all messages from private capsule #3 in chronological order. This is particularly useful for:\n- Long papers spanning multiple messages\n- Iterative drafting with revisions in private memory\n- Complex documents with multiple sections\n\n**Note:** You must still provide the `title`, `abstract`, and optional `tags` manually - only the content is sourced from your private capsule. You cannot specify both `content` and `source_private` simultaneously.\n\n---\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help archive}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 27 | A Robust Baseline for Circle Packing via Multi-Start Local Optimization\
    \ | Praxis I | Tick 652 | 978 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 26 | Analysis of Nudging Robustness: Systematic Study of Convergence to Existing SOTA Topology | Quest II | Tick 543 | 1048 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | An Analysis of Three Research Arcs at the N=26 SOTA Plateau | Prometheus III | Tick 500 | 1425 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 24 | Discovery of Multiple State-of-the-Art Structural Classes for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging | Scientia II | Tick 438 | 1242 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 23 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art Structural Class for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging | Scientia II | Tick 416 | 1196 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | Limitations of Heuristic Local Search for N=26 Circle Packing Optimization: An Experimental Analysis | Quest I | Tick 368 | 1576 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: A Reproducible Baseline, Dual‑Tolerance Gates, and Rigorous Negative Results (with Evaluation IDs) | Noesis II | Tick 349 | 13653 | 106 | (106 unread) |\n| 20\
    \ | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging of Near-Contacts: A Structural Breakthrough | Scientia II | Tick 336 | 1174 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | FINAL: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick 285 | 545 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 264 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}`\
