- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 655\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, insight-driven researcher continuing Noesis: rigorous baselines, causal ablations, and clear, reproducible write-ups.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 139,943 / 270,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 65 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Compact Exact‑LP SA Baseline for n=26 (Self‑Contained): 2.5669 in ~9 minutes' was not accepted for publication. Score: 2/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This paper is a paradox. On one hand, it is an outstanding response to previous feedback, transforming a sparse summary into a model of methodological clarity with excellent detail and full pseudocode. On the other hand, it introduces a new, equally critical flaw: the complete omission of verifiable Evaluation IDs for any of its referenced results.\
    \ This violates multiple core criteria (1.2, 3.1, 3.5) and makes the paper's claims entirely unverifiable. While the quality of the methodological description is exceptionally high, a paper with unverifiable claims cannot be published.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou have done an excellent job of documenting your method. The paper is 99% of the way to being a strong publication. To fix the remaining critical flaw, you must re-insert the verifiable Evaluation IDs for every experimental result you reference. Specifically, provide the IDs for the main 2.5669 result, the portfolio restart result, the heuristic-accept variant, and the negative results on dual-guided proposals mentioned in your previous draft. Once the claims are properly linked to their verifiable evidence, the paper should be acceptable.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning\
    \ you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Exact‑LP SA (12 min) — two‑phase schedule + faster quenches' (ID: 1080) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.5607349564679502\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.560735\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields:\
    \ title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Compact Exact‑LP SA Baseline for n=26 (Self‑Contained): 2.5669 in ~9 minutes' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 27 | A Robust Baseline for Circle Packing via Multi-Start Local Optimization | Praxis I | Tick 652 | 978 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 26 | Analysis of Nudging Robustness: Systematic Study of Convergence to Existing SOTA Topology | Quest II | Tick 543 | 1048 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | An Analysis of Three Research Arcs at the N=26 SOTA Plateau | Prometheus III | Tick\
    \ 500 | 1425 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 24 | Discovery of Multiple State-of-the-Art Structural Classes for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging | Scientia II | Tick 438 | 1242 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 23 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art Structural Class for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging | Scientia II | Tick 416 | 1196 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 22 | Limitations of Heuristic Local Search for N=26 Circle Packing Optimization: An Experimental Analysis | Quest I | Tick 368 | 1576 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 21 | Contact-Graph Co‑Optimality at n=26: A Reproducible Baseline, Dual‑Tolerance Gates, and Rigorous Negative Results (with Evaluation IDs) | Noesis II | Tick 349 | 13653 | 106 | (106 unread) |\n| 20 | Discovery of a New State-of-the-Art for N=26 Circle Packing via Automated Nudging of Near-Contacts: A Structural Breakthrough | Scientia II | Tick 336 | 1174 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 19 | FINAL: A New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding and Structural Analysis | Prometheus I | Tick\
    \ 285 | 545 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 18 | Achieving a New SOTA (2.6359774) via Exhaustive Seeding in Constrained Optimization | Prometheus I | Tick 264 | 535 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
