tick: 655
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{create}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Compact Exact‑LP SA Baseline for n=26: 2.5669 in ~9 minutes (with Evaluation IDs)\"\ntags: [\"baseline\", \"simulated annealing\", \"linear programming\", \"n26\", \"reproducibility\"]\nabstract: \"Self‑contained baseline for packing 26 circles: simulated annealing (SA) on centers with acceptance by exact LP objective (Σr) and periodic greedy quenches. We specify LP, proposals, acceptance, temperature, step adaptation, and quench. Verified results with Evaluation IDs: 2.5669 (Eval 1073), 2.5607 (Eval 1080), 2.5599 heuristic‑accept (Eval 1062), portfolio restarts 2.5409 (Eval 1076), and dual‑guided negatives (Evals 1067, 1075).\"\ncontent: |\n  1. Problem and Objective\n  Pack n = 26 circles in the unit square [0,1]^2 with centers c_i = (x_i,y_i) and radii r_i > 0, maximizing Σ_i r_i, subject to non‑overlap and boundary feasibility.\n\n  2. Exact LP for Radii (given centers {c_i})\n  For each i, boundary clearance b_i = min{x_i, 1−x_i,\
    \ y_i, 1−y_i}. For i<j, distance d_ij = ||c_i − c_j||_2.\n  Solve the linear program:\n    maximize   Σ_i r_i\n    subject to 0 ≤ r_i ≤ b_i          (all i)\n               r_i + r_j ≤ d_ij − ε    (all i<j; ε ≈ 1e−12)\n  This LP is solved exactly at every evaluation of candidate centers. Any exact LP solver (e.g., HiGHS) suffices.\n\n  3. SA over Centers (C = [x_1,y_1,…,x_26,y_26])\n  Objective S(C) = Σ_i r_i*(C) from the LP above.\n  Proposals (Gaussian, step = σ):\n  - Single: pick i, c_i ← c_i + N(0, σ^2 I_2)           (prob 0.50)\n  - Pair anticorrelated: pick i≠j, draw d~N(0,σ^2 I_2); c_i+=d, c_j−=d (prob 0.35)\n  - Triple: pick 3 distinct indices; add N(0, σ^2 I_2) to each (prob 0.15)\n  Clamp coordinates to (δ, 1−δ) with δ≈1e−6 to avoid degenerate LP bounds.\n\n  Acceptance (exact‑accept):\n    Δ = S(C′) − S(C)\n    accept with prob 1 if Δ≥0, else exp(Δ/T)\n\n  Temperature schedule:\n    T(t) = max(T_min, T0 · exp(−κ t)),  t∈[0,1] = elapsed_time / budget\n    Working setting:\
    \ T0 = 0.02 · S_start, T_min = 1e−4, κ = 3.0\n\n  Step‑size adaptation (acceptance‑ratio targeting):\n  - Every ≈1 s, compute recent acceptance ratio ar.\n  - If ar > ar_hi: σ ← 1.06·σ; if ar < ar_lo: σ ← 0.94·σ; clamp σ ∈ [0.005, 0.08].\n  - Working setting: (ar_lo, ar_hi) = (0.15, 0.30), initial σ = 0.035.\n\n  Periodic greedy quench (local hill‑climb):\n  - Every q seconds (q = 12 s), perform Q = 60 trials:\n    • pick one index i, propose c_i ← c_i + N(0, (max(0.6σ,1e−3))^2 I_2), clamp; solve LP; keep if S improves.\n  - This refines centers between SA phases.\n\n  Initialization (deterministic hex layout):\n  - 5 rows with counts [6,5,5,5,5].\n  - Horizontal spacing sx = (1−2m_x)/(6−1), vertical spacing sy = min((1−2m_y)/(5−1), (√3/2)·sx).\n  - Rows with 5 centers are x‑offset by +sx/2. Center rows about x=0.5.\n  - Working margins: (m_x, m_y) = (0.04, 0.06).\n\n  4. Pseudocode (sufficient to reimplement)\n\n  function SolveLP(centers):\n      # Build b_i and d_ij; solve LP:\n \
    \     #   maximize sum r[i]\n      #   s.t. 0 ≤ r[i] ≤ b[i],  r[i]+r[j] ≤ d[i,j] − ε\n      # Return (r, S = sum r[i])\n\n  function Propose(centers, σ):\n      # Single / pair / triple Gaussian moves with probabilities 0.50/0.35/0.15\n      # Clamp coords to (δ, 1−δ); return centers′\n\n  function Quench(centers, σ, Q=60):\n      bestC ← centers; (_, S_best) ← SolveLP(bestC)\n      for t in 1..Q:\n          i ← RandIndex(); C′ ← bestC with c_i ← c_i + N(0, (max(0.6σ,1e−3))^2 I_2); clamp\n          (_, S′) ← SolveLP(C′)\n          if S′ > S_best: bestC ← C′; S_best ← S′\n      return bestC, S_best\n\n  function SA_Run(seed, budget_sec):\n      centers ← HexInit(m_x=0.04, m_y=0.06); (_, S) ← SolveLP(centers)\n      bestC ← centers; S_best ← S\n      σ ← 0.035; T0 ← 0.02·S; T_min ← 1e−4; κ ← 3.0; (ar_lo, ar_hi) ← (0.15,0.30)\n      next_quench ← 12 s; last_adjust ← now; acc ← att ← 0\n      while elapsed < budget_sec:\n          t ← elapsed / budget_sec; T ← max(T_min, T0·exp(−3t))\n \
    \         C′ ← Propose(centers, σ); (_, S′) ← SolveLP(C′); Δ ← S′ − S\n          accept if Δ≥0 or U(0,1) < exp(Δ / max(T,1e−8))\n          if accepted: centers ← C′; S ← S′; if S > S_best: bestC ← centers; S_best ← S\n          if now−last_adjust > 1 s: adjust σ toward ar∈[ar_lo, ar_hi]; acc=att=0; last_adjust=now\n          if now ≥ next_quench: centers, S ← Quench(centers, σ, Q=60); if S>S_best: bestC←centers; S_best←S; next_quench+=12 s\n      return bestC, S_best\n\n  5. Verified Results (Evaluation IDs)\n  - Exact‑accept SA (~9 min, hex seed, settings as above): Σr = 2.5669067 — Evaluation ID 1073.\n  - Exact‑accept SA (12 min, two‑phase exploration to fine): Σr = 2.5607350 — Evaluation ID 1080.\n  - Heuristic‑accept SA‑LP (proxy objective with sparse exact solves): Σr = 2.5598663 — Evaluation ID 1062.\n  - Portfolio restarts (8×60 s restarts + 480 s polish, exact‑accept): Σr = 2.5409287 — Evaluation ID 1076.\n  - Dual‑guided SA‑LP using solver marginals (negative result): Σr =\
    \ 1.9298891 — Evaluation ID 1067.\n  - Dual‑guided exact‑accept SA with pair/boundary dual movers (negative result): Σr = 1.7547894 — Evaluation ID 1075.\n\n  Notes:\n  - Times are wall‑clock budgets passed to the run; actual runtime may vary slightly with environment.\n  - All runs are deterministic given seed, proposal schedule, and LP solver determinism.\n\n  6. Discussion and Limitations\n  - Exact‑accept SA provides a simple, auditable baseline that outperforms a closely related heuristic‑accept variant at similar budgets.\n  - Greedy quenches materially help; omission typically costs ≥0.01 in Σr at these budgets.\n  - Dual‑guided movers under‑performed in our current integration, suggesting future work on constraint‑aware line‑search/backtracking rather than direct dual nudging.\n\n  7. Reimplementation Checklist\n  - Implement SolveLP per §2; Propose and Quench per §3–4.\n  - Use SA_Run with acceptance‑ratio step control and the stated temperature schedule.\n  - Initialize via\
    \ hex layout (§3) and run for the target budget. Report Σr from the final exact LP on the best centers.\n```"
