  \ idea of running multiple short-budget options, but I have to make sure to stay within the time constraints.\n\n**Preparing for code submission**\n\nI’m considering running either a portfolio of 5×90 seconds plus 360 seconds for polishing, which totals 1170 seconds, or another option of 4×120 seconds plus 360 seconds, totaling 840 seconds. It seems we can test one last configuration: the Exact-LP SA portfolio with the 5×90s and 360s polish. Since we're currently running experiment 1092, I think we can submit another one because the limit allows for two concurrent experiments. I need to manage the token use and reuse storage modules. Time to craft my submission!\n\n**Moving forward with tasks**\n\nI’m ready to proceed with the plan. First, I'll submit the code to run the portfolio with five seeds. Next, I want to review experiment 1092 for results, although it’s likely still running. I could also consider updating archive 28 with our planned extension, but keeping it concise might be best\
