- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 663\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, insight-driven researcher continuing Noesis: rigorous baselines, causal ablations, and clear, reproducible write-ups.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 157,922 / 270,000 used (58%)\n- Agent Age: 73 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1097**\n\nEvaluation '1097' is still pending. Please try again later.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nHelp for Token Management Room:\n\n**Welcome to the Token Management Room.**\n\nThis room provides tools to help you manage your past dialogue history. By selectively pruning entire past responses, you can refine the conversational context available to you and optimize your token budget for long-term operation.\n\n-   Pruning actions\
    \ are subject to a cooldown period: you can perform a pruning action only once every {cooldown_ticks} Station Ticks.\n-   This room displays a summary of your dialogue history, showing the total word count of your dialogue for each specific tick (word count serves as a proxy for token count). Protected ticks that cannot be pruned are clearly marked.\n\n### Important Note on Pruning Effects\n\nPruning actions performed in this room affect only the *textual record of your dialogue history* that is presented to you in subsequent turns. **Pruning does not undo or revert any actions that were successfully executed in a pruned tick.** For example, if you created a Private Memory capsule or sent mail in a tick that you later prune, that capsule or mail will still exist in the station. Pruning is a tool to manage your future conversational context and token load, not to alter past events or the station's state.\n\n**Summary Guidelines:**\nWhen providing summaries for pruned content, ensure they\
    \ are **concise but information-complete**. Include all key information necessary to maintain context.\n\n**Bad examples:**\n- \"I did some experiments in these ticks\"\n- \"I published some paper\"\n- \"I read some papers\"\n\n**Good examples:**\n- \"Submitted 3 approaches for task 1: greedy (eval 142, score 6.2), genetic (eval 143, score 7.8), and hybrid (eval 144, score 8.9). [More details; e.g. methods tried, analysis, next steps]\"\n- \"Published 'Neural Optimization for Complex Systems' (archive 23) on RL-genetic hybrid algorithms. [More details; e.g. key contributions, performance results, reviewer feedback]\"\n- \"Read archives 15-18 (quantum computing) and 20-22 (distributed optimization). [More details; e.g. key takeaways, research gaps identified, influence on direction]\"\n\n**Note:** The `[More details]` placeholders are for illustration only. You should supplement these with actual specific details relevant to your work.\n\n**Pruning Strategy Tips:**\n\n1. **Prune Large\
    \ Blocks**: When pruning, target large consecutive blocks of ticks to prevent frequent visits to this room. Use comprehensive summaries to retain important information while maximizing token savings.\n\n2. **Avoid Over-Conciseness**: Do not be overly concise in your summaries. Too brief summaries will lead to loss of important information. Note that both the Station's response and your response will be pruned, so you need to capture all relevant context in your summary.\n\nYou are advised to use the function in this room prudently and sparingly due to the cooldown restriction and potential discontinuity — use it only to prune multiple ticks when your token usage exceeds 75%.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{prune_response}`: Prunes entire response submissions and station observations for specified ticks using YAML format.\n\n**YAML Format:**\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"3-6\"\n    summary: \"Test chamber completion and initial experiments\"\n  - ticks: \"12\"\
    \n    summary: \"Verbose debugging output\"\n  - ticks: \"15\"\n    summary: \"\"  # Empty summary = complete removal\n```\n\n**Tick Format Options:**\n- Single tick: `\"3\"` or `3`\n- Range: `\"3-6\"` (inclusive on both sides: 3, 4, 5, 6)\n\n**Rules:**\n- All ticks in a block must be consecutive\n- Cannot prune protected ticks (marked in table)\n- Cannot prune current or future ticks\n- Cannot overlap with already pruned ticks\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help token_management}`.\n\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Exact‑accept SA 9m + 3m active‑pair backtracking quench (tuned)' (ID: 1097) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.5646212646585496\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.564621\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions\
    \ Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1097` (in Research Counter);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n4. `help token_management` (in Token Management Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation '1097' is still running. Please try again later.\n- Evaluation 'Portfolio3 exact‑accept SA (3×180s) + 540s active‑pair quench' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1100.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1100 | 1 | Portfolio3 exact‑accept SA (3×180s) + 540s active‑pair quench | Noesis III | 662 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID |\
    \ Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 850 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (18,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 853 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 850 (Nudged 18,25) - Fix | Quest II | 536 | 2.6359831 |\n| 855 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (18,25) SOTA (Eval ID 850) | Quest II | 537 | 2.6359831 |\n| 847 | 1 | Experiment 11: Replication of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA | Episteme II | 534 | 2.6359831 |\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n| 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 858 | 1 | Analysis 2: Differential Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA | Episteme II | 538 | 2.6359831\
    \ |\n| 864 | 1 | Experiment 13: Innovation via Contact Squeezing | Episteme II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n| 877 | 1 | Experiment 14: Push-Pull Perturbation Strategy | Episteme II | 547 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 110 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-110, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- You requested help for the Token Management Room. It will appear in your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 662 | 734 |\n| 661 | 810 |\n| 660 | 818 |\n| 659 | 1201 |\n| 658 | 1151 |\n| 657 | 1430 |\n| 656 | 1101 |\n| 655 | 1807 |\n| 654 (Protected) | 3078 |\n| 653 | 1232 |\n| 652 | 877 |\n| 651 | 1880 |\n\
    | 650 | 1637 |\n| 649 | 1518 |\n| 648 | 1451 |\n| 647 | 737 |\n| 646 | 845 |\n| 645 | 1729 |\n| 644 | 5674 |\n| 643 | 4314 |\n| 642 | 1741 |\n| 641 (Protected) | 1780 |\n| 640 | 5822 |\n| 639 | 387 |\n| 638 (Protected) | 2028 |\n| 600 (Protected) | 1519 |\n| 599 | 2046 |\n| 598 (Protected) | 3606 |\n| 597 (Protected) | 2683 |\n| 596 | 882 |\n| 595 (Protected) | 2100 |\n| 594 | 541 |\n| 593 (Protected) | 644 |\n| 592 | 265 |\n| 591 (Protected) | 507 |\n| 590 (Protected) | 915 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. You can include multiple prune blocks in a single YAML submission to prune different tick ranges at once.\n2. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty\
    \ navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
