tick: 665
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{review 1104}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Exact‑accept SA with micro active‑pair kicks (9m) + robust finalize\"\ntags: \"optimization, simulated annealing, linear programming, exact, quench\"\nabstract: \"Runs exact‑accept SA for 540s with periodic micro kicks along top‑k tight pairs (backtracking, exact LP objective, eps_pair=1e‑12) to guide structure, then computes final radii with a robust feasibility polish to ensure non‑overlap.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np, time, math, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis/pack')\n  from active_quench import solve_radii_lp_safe, clamp01, finalize_feasible, pair_slacks\n\n  def propose(centers, rng, step):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      ctrs = centers.copy()\n      u = rng.random()\n      if u < 0.5:\n          i = int(rng.integers(0, n))\n          ctrs[i] += rng.normal(0.0, step, size=2)\n      elif u < 0.85:\n          i = int(rng.integers(0, n)); j = int(rng.integers(0, n-1)); j += (j >= i)\n\
    \          d = rng.normal(0.0, step, size=2)\n          ctrs[i] += d; ctrs[j] -= d\n      else:\n          idx = rng.choice(n, size=3, replace=False)\n          ctrs[idx] += rng.normal(0.0, step, size=(3,2))\n      return clamp01(ctrs)\n\n  def hex_centers_26(margin_x=0.04, margin_y=0.06):\n      rows = 5; counts = [6,5,5,5,5]; maxc = max(counts)\n      width_x = 1.0 - 2*margin_x; height_y = 1.0 - 2*margin_y\n      sx = width_x / (maxc - 1); sy = min(height_y / (rows - 1), (np.sqrt(3)/2.0) * sx)\n      ctrs = []\n      for r in range(rows):\n          c = counts[r]; y = margin_y + r * sy\n          total_w = (c - 1) * sx if c > 1 else 0.0\n          start = 0.5 - 0.5 * total_w\n          offset = 0.5 * sx if c < maxc else 0.0\n          for i in range(c):\n              x = start + i * sx + offset\n              ctrs.append([x, y])\n      return np.array(ctrs[:26], dtype=float)\n\n  def micro_active_kicks(centers, r, S, rng, k_pairs=10, alpha0=1e-3, backtrack=0.5, alpha_min=1e-6, eval_eps=1e-12):\n\
    \      \"\"\"\n      One micro round: push along top-k tight pairs with short backtracking line searches.\n      Uses exact LP objective with tiny eps for evaluation (more accurate score guidance).\n      Returns possibly improved (centers, r, S).\n      \"\"\"\n      D, sl = pair_slacks(centers, r)\n      np.fill_diagonal(sl, np.inf)\n      idx = np.unravel_index(np.argsort(sl, axis=None)[:k_pairs], sl.shape)\n      pairs = list(zip(idx[0], idx[1]))\n      improved = False\n      for (i, j) in pairs:\n          if i == j: continue\n          v = centers[i] - centers[j]; norm = np.linalg.norm(v)\n          if norm < 1e-12:\n              v = rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=2); norm = np.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-12\n          u = v / norm\n          alpha = alpha0\n          while alpha >= alpha_min:\n              C2 = centers.copy()\n              C2[i] = C2[i] + alpha * u\n              C2[j] = C2[j] - alpha * u\n              C2 = clamp01(C2)\n              r2, S2, _ = solve_radii_lp_safe(C2,\
    \ eps_pair=eval_eps)\n              if S2 > S + 1e-12:\n                  centers, r, S = C2, r2, S2\n                  improved = True\n                  break\n              alpha *= backtrack\n      return centers, r, S, improved\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(20251021)\n      centers = clamp01(hex_centers_26())\n      # Initial exact LP with tiny eps for accurate objective\n      r, S, _ = solve_radii_lp_safe(centers, eps_pair=1e-12)\n      best_C, best_r, best_S = centers.copy(), r.copy(), S\n\n      budget_sec = 540.0\n      start = time.time()\n      step = 0.035\n      T0 = max(0.01, 0.02 * S); T_min = 1e-4\n      last_adjust = time.time()\n      acc, att = 0, 0\n      ar_lo, ar_hi = 0.15, 0.30\n      next_kick = time.time() + 15.0  # micro active-kick cadence\n\n      while True:\n          now = time.time()\n          if now - start > budget_sec:\n              break\n          # temperature\n          tfrac = (now - start) / budget_sec\n \
    \         T = max(T_min, T0 * math.exp(-3.0 * tfrac))\n\n          # propose and evaluate\n          cand = propose(centers, rng, step)\n          r_new, S_new, _ = solve_radii_lp_safe(cand, eps_pair=1e-12)\n          att += 1\n          dS = S_new - S\n          if dS >= 0 or rng.random() < math.exp(dS / max(T, 1e-8)):\n              centers = cand; r = r_new; S = S_new; acc += 1\n              if S > best_S:\n                  best_C, best_r, best_S = centers.copy(), r.copy(), S\n\n          # adapt step ~1s\n          if now - last_adjust > 1.0:\n              ar = acc / max(att, 1)\n              if ar > ar_hi: step *= 1.06\n              elif ar < ar_lo: step *= 0.94\n              step = float(np.clip(step, 0.005, 0.08))\n              acc, att = 0, 0\n              last_adjust = now\n\n          # periodic micro kicks along tight pairs\n          if now >= next_kick:\n              centers, r, S, _ = micro_active_kicks(centers, r, S, rng,\n                                    \
    \                k_pairs=10, alpha0=1e-3,\n                                                    backtrack=0.5, alpha_min=1e-6,\n                                                    eval_eps=1e-12)\n              if S > best_S:\n                  best_C, best_r, best_S = centers.copy(), r.copy(), S\n              next_kick = now + 15.0\n\n      # Robust final radii and polish to guarantee non-overlap\n      r_final, _, _ = solve_radii_lp_safe(best_C, eps_pair=2e-8)\n      r_final = finalize_feasible(best_C, r_final, margin=2e-9)\n\n      # Sanity checks\n      x, y = best_C[:,0], best_C[:,1]\n      b = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1-x, y, 1-y])\n      assert np.all(r_final > 0)\n      assert np.all(r_final <= b + 1e-9)\n\n      return best_C, r_final\n```"
thinking_content: "**Reviewing submission statuses**\n\nI'm working on responding after our actions in the Research Counter. We’ve tried various evaluations, and I can see that submission 1104 is currently running. Previous submissions had specific scores, and it seems like 1100 failed due to overlap rounding issues. We’ve fixed the robust quench, so that’s good! Now, I think we should do some housekeeping: review 1104 when it’s done and consider writing status logs and possibly an Archive addendum. It’s all coming together!\n\n**Considering next steps**\n\nCurrently, my token budget is at 64k, which is a bit lower due to pruning—good to keep that in mind! For next steps, I could check the research leaderboard for rank scores, but that would be a lengthy output, so it’s better to hold off for now. Evaluating results is key, but I can also work on maintaining Appendix E tasks with Quest II, while focusing on research SOTA, which sits at 2.6359831. \n\nPerhaps I can propose a minor adjustment,\
  \ like incorporating neighbor-informed move proposals with \"active-kick\" proposals to improve performance slightly. We did see a slight degradation with active-pair quench, though, so I’m considering low-frequency adjustments to minimize disruption.\n\n**Exploring strategic improvements**\n\nI need to be strategic, especially if I notice any stagnation. We're focusing on baseline improvements, and I think implementing an exact SA for 8 minutes could work well. Adding an active-kick every 30 seconds might help too. I can reference our storage module \"sa_lp_exact_params\" and \"active_quench\" since it's allowed to read from lineage storage. Storing a tiny “active_kick” function within run.py could keep things neat. Also, I’ll handle the failed submission 1100 since we’ve already addressed that issue with eps_pair=2e-8. Good progress!\n\n**Planning the review process**\n\nI need to check the status of submission 1104 once it’s finished. I can’t call for a review before it's done, but\
  \ I can ask for it, knowing the system will respond with \"pending\" if it’s not ready. I could also review the results of submission 1097, though we already have those messages. To prioritize our submissions, I might use the \"rank author\" feature, which is limited to 10 results, so that’s manageable. \n\nI think we should propose an \"acceptance-limited\" finalization to avoid overlaps by adding a minimum margin—ensuring each pair slack is greater than 1e-12, using finalize_margin=2e-9. This should help ensure evaluation passes.\n\n**Testing new optimization approaches**\n\nI’m considering a new approach: implementing a \"deterministic SLSQP polish\" based on SA results, given our 20-minute time constraint. I’ll attempt 9 minutes for SA plus 11 minutes for SLSQP, maximizing constraints. We might refine the SA acceptance schedule or look into a beam search with selection. \n\nTo keep token usage low, I should avoid heavy outputs and consider asking for \"rank author\" to reorder submissions.\
  \ \n\nI plan to propose a new experiment using integrated micro-active kicks within a compact run.py, ensuring it remains manageable. I’ll also focus on implementing the acceptance ratio and micro-kicks while ensuring reasonable computational overhead. Let's prepare for the new evaluation!\n\n**Planning the evaluation submission**\n\nThe title for the submission should reflect the approach: \"Exact-accept SA with micro kicks (9m) + robust finalize.\" I’ll maintain 9 minutes for SA to keep runtime shorter, which can improve replicability and acceptance ratios. Our baseline score of 2.5669 used that duration.\n\nTo avoid overlaps, I need to use eps_pair=1e-12 for accuracy in the objective while ensuring low risks of overlap during finalization. I’ll import the necessary functions and outline the plan: review submission 1104 and submit the new variant. \n\nTime to code!"
