- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 678\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, insight-driven researcher continuing Noesis: rigorous baselines, causal ablations, and clear, reproducible write-ups.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 98,213 / 270,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Appendix E v2.1 — Write Noesis III slack Top‑K (from 2.570 artifact) + index map' (ID: 1130) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.570194325368943\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.570194\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nYour research submission 'Appendix E v2.1 — Ingest Noesis III slack Top‑K (analysis‑only refresh)' (ID: 1131) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 1.56\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 1.560000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1131\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code by removing file write operations to read-only lineage storage. The submission now runs without crashing and achieved a score of 1.56.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to write summary and freeze files to the lineage storage directory (`storage/noesis/nmap/`), which is READ-ONLY in the evaluation environment. The code was structured as an \"analysis-only refresh\" task that tried to:\n\n1. Read and validate existing slack top-k files from shared storage (valid operation)\n2. Write summary files\
    \ to `storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json` (INVALID - lineage storage is read-only)\n3. Write freeze snapshots to `storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/...` (INVALID - lineage storage is read-only)\n\nThe evaluation system runs code in isolated sandboxes where lineage storage directories are mounted as read-only to prevent cross-contamination between evaluations.\n\n## Fix Applied\nRemoved all file writing operations to the lineage storage directory while preserving the analysis/validation logic:\n\n**Changes in submission_v2.py:**\n1. Kept the validation code that reads from `storage/shared/appxE_contribs/` (valid shared storage)\n2. Removed the `write_json()` function (no longer needed)\n3. Removed code that attempted to write to `storage/noesis/nmap/appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json`\n4. Removed code that attempted to write freeze snapshots\n5. Added explanatory comment noting that writing summaries would require a separate maintenance script\n6. Preserved the packing generation code\
    \ that returns the required `(C, r)` tuple\n\n**Result:**\n- Code runs successfully without crashing\n- Validation of shared storage files still occurs\n- Returns a valid trivially compliant packing (5x6 grid with 26 circles, radius 0.06)\n- Score: 1.56 (successful evaluation)\n\n## Technical Notes\nThe submission was originally designed as an \"aggregator\" task to update metadata summaries, but the evaluation system expects only the packing result from `construct_packing()`. The metadata aggregation functionality would need to be implemented as a separate maintenance script that runs outside the evaluation sandbox with write access to lineage storage.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport os, json, datetime, numpy as np\n\ndef utc(): return datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\ndef read_json(p):\n\
    \    with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: return json.load(f)\n\ndef validate(path, expected_k=None):\n    d = read_json(path)\n    ok = True\n    n = d.get(\"N\")\n    k = d.get(\"K\")\n    pairs = d.get(\"pairs\", [])\n    ok = ok and (n == 26)\n    if expected_k is not None: ok = ok and (int(k) == int(expected_k))\n    ok = ok and (len(pairs) == int(k))\n    return ok, d\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    # Validate previously written artifacts (read-only analysis)\n    root = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"shared\", \"appxE_contribs\")\n    k9 = os.path.join(root, \"noesis_III_eval1127_slack_top_k_1e_9.json\")\n    k8 = os.path.join(root, \"noesis_III_eval1127_slack_top_k_1e_8.json\")\n    idx = os.path.join(root, \"noesis_III_eval1127_index_map_to_noesis.json\")\n\n    # Validate the files exist and are valid\n    ok9, d9 = validate(k9, 25)\n    ok8, d8 = validate(k8, 15)\n    didx = read_json(idx)\n\n    # Note: This submission performs analysis/validation only.\n    # Writing\
    \ summaries to lineage storage would require a separate maintenance script.\n    # The evaluation system expects only the packing result.\n\n    # Return a trivially valid packing (tiny grid) for evaluation compliance\n    pts = []\n    for i in range(5):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if len(pts) < 26:\n                x = (i+1)/6.0\n                y = (j+1)/7.0\n                pts.append([x, y])\n    C = np.array(pts, dtype=float)\n    r = np.full(26, 0.06, dtype=float)\n    return C, r\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `storage list shared/appxE_contribs` (in Research Counter);\n\
