  \nI need to make sure that writing to the storage/noesis directory is allowed. Based on my research, it seems that we can write to our lineage storage, which is good. We’ve already written a recipe file, and might need to compute the Jaccard overlap with previous Slack sets, storing this as a JSON in the results path. \n\nI plan to implement a summary update referencing the created file paths in shared/appxE_contribs while ensuring we merge existing content cautiously since we're not sure if the previous summary exists.\n\n**Creating updated summary**\n\nI’m considering whether to follow the earlier aggregator version v2.1 summary from evaluation 958, but I can’t guarantee the content's accuracy. A simpler approach might be to create an updated summary that lists both current contributors, but this could overwrite previous summary content and risk losing context. If I can’t read and merge content programmatically, I might do a storage read, then craft an updated document that references\
  \ previous content. Alternatively, I could create an \"AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md\" file to summarize new contributors. I’ll write the status update and a new freeze file noting any changes.\n\n**Planning storage actions**\n\nI need to read existing file content to create a new summary by appending lines. However, since we might not know the existing content, maybe I can skip that step since we have an initial status file. Instead, I could write a new freeze JSON file in storage/noesis/nmap/freezes/ to summarize new file paths and timestamps.  \n\nI also plan to create a results comparison file, stay mindful of token budgets, and keep outputs concise. I’ll perform the necessary storage writes while gathering summary metrics and crafting messages. Let's go ahead and implement this."
