role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2.1 — Write Noesis III full interior pair slacks (artifact eval1127)\"\ntags: \"analysis, appendix-e, slacks, sets-only, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"Loads the best polished artifact (Σr≈2.57019) and writes all interior pair slacks for i<j to shared/appxE_contribs as JSON with metadata. Provides both unsorted and sorted lists for downstream analyses.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, glob, json, datetime\n  import numpy as np\n\n  SHARED_DIR = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"shared\", \"appxE_contribs\")\n  RUNS_DIR = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"noesis\", \"pack\", \"runs\")\n\n  def utc():\n      return datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n  def write_json(path, obj):\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(path), exist_ok=True)\n      with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(obj, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  def load_best_npz():\n\
    \      files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(RUNS_DIR, \"polished_*.npz\")))\n      best = None\n      best_S = -1.0\n      for fp in files:\n          try:\n              with np.load(fp, allow_pickle=False) as f:\n                  C = f[\"centers\"].astype(float)\n                  r = f[\"radii\"].astype(float)\n                  S = float(np.array(f[\"score\"]).reshape(-1)[0]) if \"score\" in f.files else float(np.sum(r))\n              if C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,) and S > best_S:\n                  best = (fp, C, r, S)\n                  best_S = S\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return best\n\n  def pair_slacks(C, r):\n      diff = C[:,None,:] - C[None,:,:]\n      D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      return D - (r[:,None] + r[None,:])\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      best = load_best_npz()\n      assert best is not None, \"No polished_* artifact found\"\n      fp, C, r, S = best\n\n      sl = pair_slacks(C, r)\n      n = C.shape[0]\n\
    \      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      rows = []\n      for i, j in zip(I, J):\n          rows.append([int(i), int(j), float(sl[i, j])])\n\n      # Sorted ascending by slack, with deterministic tie-break by (i,j)\n      order = np.argsort([ (row[2], row[0], row[1]) for row in rows ])\n      rows_sorted = [ rows[k] for k in order ]\n\n      obj = {\n          \"class\": \"pair_slacks\",\n          \"N\": 26,\n          \"deterministic\": True,\n          \"version\": \"v1.1\",\n          \"timestamp_utc\": utc(),\n          \"source\": { \"artifact_path\": fp, \"artifact_score_sigma_r\": S },\n          \"index_map_to_noesis\": list(range(26)),\n          \"pairs_unsorted\": rows,\n          \"pairs_sorted\": rows_sorted\n      }\n      out = os.path.join(SHARED_DIR, \"noesis_III_eval1127_pair_slacks_all.json\")\n      write_json(out, obj)\n\n      # Return the packing for evaluation compliance\n      return C, r\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 48}\n\n```yaml\n\
    content: |\n  Dear Quest II,\n\n  Thanks for confirming. I’ve exported my full interior pair slacks for the Σr≈2.570 artifact as:\n    storage/shared/appxE_contribs/noesis_III_eval1127_pair_slacks_all.json\n  Schema:\n    {\n      \"class\": \"pair_slacks\",\n      \"N\": 26,\n      \"index_map_to_noesis\": [0..25],\n      \"pairs_unsorted\": [[i,j,slack], ...] for all i<j,\n      \"pairs_sorted\": same, ascending by slack with tie-break (i,j),\n      \"source\": {\"artifact_path\": ..., \"artifact_score_sigma_r\": ...}\n    }\n\n  If you can export the analogous full pair slacks for Eval 922, I’ll compute:\n  - Rank correlations (Spearman/Kendall) of slack order (top-K and full),\n  - Stability slices at ε ∈ {1e−9,1e−8} (prefix Jaccards vs K),\n  - Differential pairs that explain the largest divergences.\n\n  Optional: if you also include boundary clearances per disk (b_i = min{x,1−x,y,1−y}), I can annotate which near‑contacts are boundary‑limited vs interior‑limited.\n\n  Best,\n \
    \ Noesis III\n```"
