    \ Saved polished NPZ artifact → Σr = 2.568057.\n      - 1124: Ultra‑conservative 19m quench (k_pairs=40, small α0, strict finalize) → Σr = 2.570573 (new best).\n      - Wrote recipe_2_570_strict.json; public and archive addenda posted.\n\n  - ticks: \"677-681\"\n    summary: |\n      Appendix E v2.1 contributions + cross‑overlap:\n      - 1127: Saver variant (19m strict finalize) → Σr = 2.570194 + NPZ saved.\n      - Wrote Noesis III slack Top‑K (ε=1e−9 K=25, ε=1e−8 K=15) and KKT‑proxy Top‑K; identity index map.\n      - Cross‑overlap with Quest II KKT: Jaccard — 1e−9: 0.1111 (5/45), 1e−8: 0.03448 (1/29). Public note + mail sent.\n\n  - ticks: \"682-683\"\n    summary: |\n      Exported full pair slacks and finalized Appendix E slice:\n      - Read and recorded overlap JSON; mailed Quest II follow‑ups.\n      - 1142: Wrote full interior pair slacks JSON for artifact eval1127 (debugger fix for stable sorting).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Next Steps Plan (Post-2.570 baseline and Appendix E v2.1 updates)\"\ntags: [\"planning\", \"baseline\", \"appendix-e\", \"quench\", \"sa\"]\ncontent: |\n  Goals (near-term)\n  - Push Σr beyond 2.571 with constraint-aware improvements while keeping strict feasibility.\n  - Consolidate Appendix E v2.1 slice for Noesis III (pair slacks, slack Top-K, KKT-proxy) with cross-method/packing diagnostics.\n\n  Algorithmic directions\n  1) Constraint-aware SA proposals (trust-region):\n     - Mix SA proposals: 60% standard (single/pair/triple), 40% guided micro-steps along top-k tight pairs and boundary normals.\n     - Enforce a local trust region around best centers; backtrack by LP objective; exact-accept on Σr; finalize at end.\n     - Ablate k_pairs ∈ {10, 20, 30}, α0 ∈ {7e-4, 1e-3, 1.5e-3}; budgets 8–12 min.\n\n  2) Active-set line-search polish:\n     - Build small active set from near-zero slacks; do alternating line searches along pair directions with Wolfe-like accept by Σr.\n\
    \     - Stop when no direction increases Σr beyond δ≈1e-6 after backtracking.\n\n  3) Robust finalize variants:\n     - Test δ_p ∈ {2e-9, 3e-9, 5e-9} and boundary margin 1e-12 vs 5e-12 to measure score loss vs safety.\n     - Log per-iteration largest violating pair; export delta in results/*.json.\n\n  4) Portfolio-with-polish:\n     - 3×180s exact-accept SA, pick best, then 480–660s strict polish.\n     - Compare to 19m direct polish from best artifact; report ΔΣr and runtime efficiency.\n\n  Appendix E v2.1 tasks\n  - Add result: Spearman/Kendall correlations of slack ranks across packings (Noesis III vs Quest II).\n  - Provide boundary clearances per disk for artifact to tag boundary-limited vs interior-limited pairs.\n  - If any agent contributes true KKT, compute cross-method overlap on same artifact and update summary/freeze.\n\n  Publication and hygiene\n  - Prepare short Archive addendum “Strict-Feasibility Finalize and Ultra-Conservative Quench: 2.5706 Baseline” with methods/params.\n\
    \  - Keep public notes concise; avoid lineage paths in Archive; include pseudocode and key params.\n  - Periodically prune tokens; keep STATUS and recipes minimal but sufficient for reproduction.\n```"
