- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2.1 — Ingest Noesis III (Eval1127) Top‑K/Pair‑Slacks and Overlap vs Quest II KKT (analysis-only)\"\ntags: \"analysis, appendix-e, aggregator, sets-only, overlap\"\nabstract: \"Adds Noesis III Eval1127 contributions (slack Top‑K, KKT‑proxy Top‑K, full interior pair slacks) to Appendix E v2.1 summary; computes Jaccard overlaps vs Quest II KKT Top‑K (ε∈{1e−9,1e−8}); writes summary, freeze, and results. Returns a valid trivial packing for evaluator compliance.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, datetime\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def utc_now():\n      return datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n  def ensure_dir(p):\n      os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def read_json(path):\n      with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          return json.load(f)\n\n  def write_json(path, obj):\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(path))\n      with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n         \
    \ json.dump(obj, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n  def append_status(path, lines):\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(path))\n      with open(path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          f.write(lines)\n\n  def extract_pairs(data):\n      # Accepts dict with \"pairs\", \"pairs_sorted\", or a raw list; returns set of (i,j)\n      pairs = []\n      if isinstance(data, dict):\n          if \"pairs_sorted\" in data and isinstance(data[\"pairs_sorted\"], list):\n              pairs = data[\"pairs_sorted\"]\n          elif \"pairs\" in data and isinstance(data[\"pairs\"], list):\n              pairs = data[\"pairs\"]\n          else:\n              # find first list of list-likes\n              for v in data.values():\n                  if isinstance(v, list) and v and isinstance(v[0], (list,tuple)) and len(v[0]) >= 2:\n                      pairs = v\n                      break\n      elif isinstance(data, list):\n          pairs = data\n      S = set()\n      for\
    \ it in pairs:\n          if isinstance(it, (list, tuple)) and len(it) >= 2:\n              i, j = int(it[0]), int(it[1])\n              if i == j: \n                  continue\n              if i < j: \n                  S.add((i,j))\n              else: \n                  S.add((j,i))\n      return S\n\n  def jaccard(a, b):\n      if not a and not b:\n          return 1.0\n      inter = len(a & b)\n      union = len(a | b)\n      return inter / union if union else 0.0\n\n  def load_topk(path):\n      if not os.path.exists(path):\n          return None, None\n      d = read_json(path)\n      S = extract_pairs(d)\n      meta = {\n          \"path\": path,\n          \"K\": len(S),\n          \"N\": d.get(\"N\", None),\n          \"class\": d.get(\"class\", None),\n          \"method\": d.get(\"method\", None),\n          \"version\": d.get(\"version\", None)\n      }\n      return S, meta\n\n  def main():\n      ts = utc_now()\n      shared = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"shared\", \"\
    appxE_contribs\")\n      out_root = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"noesis\", \"nmap\")\n      freezes_dir = os.path.join(out_root, \"freezes\")\n      results_dir = os.path.join(out_root, \"results\")\n      ensure_dir(out_root); ensure_dir(freezes_dir); ensure_dir(results_dir)\n\n      status_path = os.path.join(out_root, \"AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md\")\n      summary_path = os.path.join(out_root, \"appendix_E_summary_v2_1.json\")\n\n      # Noesis III (Eval1127) files\n      n_slack_9 = os.path.join(shared, \"noesis_III_eval1127_slack_top_k_1e_9.json\")\n      n_slack_8 = os.path.join(shared, \"noesis_III_eval1127_slack_top_k_1e_8.json\")\n      n_kkt_9   = os.path.join(shared, \"noesis_III_eval1127_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json\")\n      n_kkt_8   = os.path.join(shared, \"noesis_III_eval1127_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json\")\n      n_pairs   = os.path.join(shared, \"noesis_III_eval1127_pair_slacks_all.json\")\n      n_index   = os.path.join(shared, \"noesis_III_eval1127_index_map_to_noesis.json\")  # expected\
    \ identity\n\n      # Quest II KKT (Eval922)\n      q_kkt_9 = os.path.join(shared, \"quest_II_eval922_replica_kkt_top_k_1e_9.json\")\n      q_kkt_8 = os.path.join(shared, \"quest_II_eval922_replica_kkt_top_k_1e_8.json\")\n\n      missing = [p for p in [n_slack_9, n_slack_8, n_kkt_9, n_kkt_8, n_pairs, n_index, q_kkt_9, q_kkt_8] if not os.path.exists(p)]\n      if missing:\n          append_status(status_path, f\"\\n[{ts}] WARN: Missing files for NoesisIII ingest: {missing}\\n\")\n\n      # Load sets where present\n      NS9, NS9m = load_topk(n_slack_9)\n      NS8, NS8m = load_topk(n_slack_8)\n      NK9, NK9m = load_topk(n_kkt_9)\n      NK8, NK8m = load_topk(n_kkt_8)\n      Q9, Q9m   = load_topk(q_kkt_9)\n      Q8, Q8m   = load_topk(q_kkt_8)\n\n      # Overlaps\n      overlaps = {}\n      if NS9 is not None and Q9 is not None:\n          overlaps[\"slack_1e_9_vs_quest_kkt_1e_9\"] = jaccard(NS9, Q9)\n      if NS8 is not None and Q8 is not None:\n          overlaps[\"slack_1e_8_vs_quest_kkt_1e_8\"\
    ] = jaccard(NS8, Q8)\n      if NK9 is not None and Q9 is not None:\n          overlaps[\"kktproxy_1e_9_vs_quest_kkt_1e_9\"] = jaccard(NK9, Q9)\n      if NK8 is not None and Q8 is not None:\n          overlaps[\"kktproxy_1e_8_vs_quest_kkt_1e_8\"] = jaccard(NK8, Q8)\n\n      # Update summary\n      try:\n          summary = read_json(summary_path) if os.path.exists(summary_path) else {}\n      except Exception:\n          summary = {}\n      if \"contributors\" not in summary or not isinstance(summary[\"contributors\"], dict):\n          summary[\"contributors\"] = {}\n      key = \"noesis_III_eval1127\"\n      summary[\"contributors\"][key] = {\n          \"artifact_eval_id\": 1127,\n          \"index_map\": n_index if os.path.exists(n_index) else None,\n          \"files\": {\n              \"slack_top_k_1e_9\": n_slack_9 if os.path.exists(n_slack_9) else None,\n              \"slack_top_k_1e_8\": n_slack_8 if os.path.exists(n_slack_8) else None,\n              \"kkt_top_k_1e_9\": n_kkt_9\
    \ if os.path.exists(n_kkt_9) else None,\n              \"kkt_top_k_1e_8\": n_kkt_8 if os.path.exists(n_kkt_8) else None,\n              \"pair_slacks\": n_pairs if os.path.exists(n_pairs) else None\n          },\n          \"overlap_vs_quest_eval922_kkt\": overlaps\n      }\n      summary[\"updated_at_utc\"] = ts\n      summary[\"version\"] = \"v2.1\"\n      write_json(summary_path, summary)\n\n      # Freeze and results\n      freeze = {\n          \"version\": \"v2.1\",\n          \"refreshed_at_utc\": ts,\n          \"refresh_source\": \"Noesis III Eval1127 ingest\",\n          \"contributors_delta\": { key: summary[\"contributors\"][key] }\n      }\n      write_json(os.path.join(freezes_dir, f\"appendix_E_summary_v2_1_refresh_noesisIII_eval1127_{ts.replace(':','').replace('-','').replace('T','_')}.json\"), freeze)\n\n      write_json(os.path.join(results_dir, \"noesisIII_eval1127_compare_v2_1_refresh.json\"), {\n          \"contributor\": key,\n          \"overlap_jaccard\": overlaps,\n\
    \          \"meta\": {\n              \"noesis_slack_1e_9\": NS9m, \"noesis_slack_1e_8\": NS8m,\n              \"noesis_kkt_1e_9\": NK9m,   \"noesis_kkt_1e_8\": NK8m,\n              \"quest_kkt_1e_9\": Q9m,     \"quest_kkt_1e_8\": Q8m\n          },\n          \"updated_at_utc\": ts\n      })\n\n      append_status(status_path, f\"\\n[{ts}] Ingested Noesis III Eval1127 Top‑K and pair slacks; overlaps vs Quest II KKT: {overlaps}\\n\")\n      # Return a valid trivial packing\n      centers, radii = [], []\n      r = 0.06\n      for i in range(5):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if len(centers) < 26:\n                  centers.append([0.1 + i*0.2, 0.1 + j*0.15])\n                  radii.append(r)\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.array(radii, float)\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning next steps**


  I’m considering our next actions in the Research Counter. Right now, submission 1153 is running, and I need to monitor the results to see if they improve past our target of 2.571. I’ll also coordinate the ingestion of Appendix E for Quest II when new contributions come in. Our token budget looks good at 71k out of 270k. Immediate tasks include reviewing evaluation 1149 results and implementing some functions to finalize our processes. I''ll also keep track of some pair slack files we''ve written.


  **Checking next actions**


  I typically need to ensure station actions are in place, like checking our storage for polished files such as ''polished_*.npz''. I think we saved those earlier, but I should confirm that the load_best_npz function works. Our current token usage is at 26%, which is good. I’m considering updating the Appendix E aggregator to include our contributions, but I need to be cautious about scoreboard entries. Maybe I should prepare the aggregator refresh code that merges files but might be better to wait for now.


  **Updating memory and archive**


  I can create a public memory update to summarize our new best of 2.570625 since we already posted an update. I need to check the archive as #28 was accepted, and the summary shows that it exists with details about the baseline. I might also want to add an addendum updating to 2.5706 and outlining the finalize and quench parameter changes. Since the archive allows authors to reply, I''ll go ahead and add that detail. For next steps, I’ll implement ''active_quench'' improvements using methods like the golden section or backtracking.


  **Checking storage and saving artifacts**


  I need to check the storage list for ''noesis/pack/runs'' to make sure the polished_*.npz files exist. This will help verify we have the best artifact loaded. I could write a ''saver'' utility to save the new polished artifact after the 1149 run, but our current run code doesn''t save anything. Previously, we noted a "Saver variant" for NPZ saving, but it looks like nothing was saved in this instance. Implementing a ''post-run saver'' could be beneficial, allowing us to store results in the specified format.


  **Preparing aggregator submission**


  If no polished_* files exist, I''ll fallback to running a 6-minute SA plus quench, but I should confirm we have at least one polished file saved. Next, I''d like to propose an analysis-only aggregator that merges our contributions—specifically, the Noesis III pair slacks with Quest II data. To do this, I’ll re-use previously created aggregator code and implement functions to compute Jaccard metrics. I''ll structure my submission to ensure compliance and maintain clarity, while also preparing to update public memory once all contributions are integrated. Let''s move forward with the code!


  **Finalizing aggregator work**


  I need to keep an eye on the results for submission 1153, but right now my priority is to focus on crafting the aggregator. It''s good to stay organized and ensure everything is in place for that. I want to finalize my work on it to make sure it meets our requirements. Let’s get it done efficiently!'
