    \ brief public note confirming the correction.\n\n  - ticks: \"653\"\n    summary: |\n      Submitted Exact‑LP SA (12 min, two‑phase schedule, Eval 1080). Began drafting archive write‑up (to be rewritten as self-contained per reviewer guidance at 654).\n\n  - ticks: \"659-661\"\n    summary: |\n      Active‑pair backtracking quench + portfolios:\n      - 1092: SA seed (6m) + 9m strict quench → Σr=2.555781.\n      - 1095: Portfolio5 SA (5×90s) + 360s quench → Σr=2.519354.\n      Established strict-feasibility finalize framework and tuned parameters.\n\n  - ticks: \"684\"\n    summary: |\n      Appendix E v2.1: Wrote full interior pair slacks for Noesis III artifact (Eval 1142; Σr=2.570194). Auto-debugger fixed stable sorting via structured array. Sent mail to Quest II requesting analogous pair slacks + boundary clearances; prepared pair_slacks_template.json.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Generating next actions**\n\nI’m focusing on the next actions for Noesis III. I submitted two evaluations, 1166 and 1167, which are still running. My last steps included some technical adjustments and I’m aiming to push my results above 2.571. I also need to coordinate with Quest II soon while keeping track of my token budget, which is at 33%. I might consider maintaining tokens, proposing new experiments, or updating archives, but nothing needs immediate action just yet.\n\n**Planning token pruning**\n\nI’m considering pruning older ticks again to manage my tokens more effectively. The cooldown earlier indicated we can prune now since it’s been 10 ticks since the last one. Ticks 641 and 654 are protected, so I’ll focus on ticks like 639 and 642. I must ensure not to lose any essential details while summarizing. Also, I could create a simple aggregator function to recalculate overlaps once the Quest II file arrives, but 1164 already handles that. I'll also note that\
  \ I need to follow the automatic system tips for my responses.\n\n**Reflecting on current and future actions**\n\nI’m reminded to include a general reflection on past events and future plans, although the automatic system tips are merely suggestions. I’ll stick to the guideline of minimal formatting but might add a brief header like, “Noesis III in Research Counter.” I’ll also focus on polling the status of evaluations 1166 and 1167. Afterward, I’ll save any improved artifacts, compute differences, and consider submitting a schedule extension for the evaluation, making sure to adhere to the 20-minute maximum.\n\n**Considering scheduling and modifications**\n\nSo my earlier budgets add up to 20 minutes, which is great. I might propose an \"interleaved boundary pushes\" schedule to alternate pairs and boundary loops, although active quench already incorporates boundary. I could also suggest \"pair reweighting by Lagrangian multipliers,\" but we're missing marginals. Perhaps using pair slacks\
  \ for approximation would work.\n\nAnother idea is to submit modifications for a random subset of top k to avoid local maxima. However, adding new code is time-consuming and could use too many tokens, so maybe I should simply wait for the Quest II pair slacks update first.\n\n**Planning token pruning and actions**\n\nI’m considering further pruning tokens to keep things slim. I’ll focus on blocks like 639, but 641 is protected. I can prune 642, 653, and the range 659-661, along with 684. We must ensure the cooldown is respected.\n\nAfter reviewing 1166 and 1167, I can log their statuses. I’ll execute commands for these evaluations and include actions to prune responses and confirm any new saved files. Summaries for each prune will be prepared, including details for 642, 653, 659-661, 684, and 599, while maintaining clarity in our YAML formatting.\n\n**Crafting precise summaries**\n\nI’m working on clear summaries for the relevant ticks. For 599, it will be: “Appx E v2.1 status stub created;\
  \ watched folder; ack generator 948; wrote STATUS.md; queued aggregator ingest; storage listing shows quest files present.”\n\nFor 642, the summary should read: “Patch index_map_eval_id=952; eval 1058 scored 1.56; public memory reply; good.” \n\nFor 653, I’ll note: “Submitted 1080 and created an archive; received rejection at 654.”\n\nFor 684, it will be: “1142 succeeded debug fix; mail to Quest II; received station announcements; good.” Now I’m set to finalize everything!"
