parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 698\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, insight-driven researcher continuing Noesis: rigorous baselines, causal ablations, and clear, reproducible write-ups.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 81,325 / 270,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 108 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Appendix E v2.1 — Ingest Quest latest slacks+clearances; rank‑corr and Top‑K overlaps vs NoesisIII Eval1127' (ID: 1173) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 1.56\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 1.560000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1173\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed TypeError in f-string formatting that prevented code\
    \ execution.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a malformed f-string on line 63-64 of the submission:\n```python\nf\"\\n[{ts}] Rank‑corr computed vs Quest latest: rho={rho:.6f if rho is not None else float('nan')}, J@25={j25:.6f}, J@15={j15:.6f}\\n\"\n```\n\nThe issue: The conditional expression `rho:.6f if rho is not None else float('nan')` is syntactically incorrect. Python tries to apply the `.6f` format specifier to `rho` before evaluating the conditional, which fails when `rho` is `None` because `NoneType` doesn't support format strings.\n\nError message:\n```\nTypeError: unsupported format string passed to NoneType.__format__\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the f-string formatting to handle `None` values properly by pre-computing the string representation:\n\n```python\n# NEW: Compute string representation first\nrho_str = f\"{rho:.6f}\" if rho is not None else \"nan\"\nappend_status(status_path, f\"\\n[{ts}] Rank‑corr computed vs Quest latest: rho={rho_str}, J@25={j25:.6f},\
    \ J@15={j15:.6f}\\n\")\n```\n\nThis approach:\n1. Evaluates the conditional first\n2. If `rho` is not None, formats it as a float with 6 decimal places\n3. If `rho` is None, uses the string \"nan\"\n4. Uses the pre-computed string in the final f-string\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Status**: Code runs successfully without crashing\n- **Score**: 1.56\n- **Files Modified**: Only the main submission code (no lineage files needed modification)\n\nThe fix is minimal, surgical, and preserves all the original logic while properly handling the None case for the Spearman correlation coefficient.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport os, json, datetime, numpy as np\n\ndef utc_now():\n    return datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\ndef ensure_dir(p): os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n\
    \ndef read_json(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n\ndef append_status(path, lines):\n    ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(path))\n    with open(path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(lines)\n\ndef detect_pairs(data):\n    # Return dict {(i,j): slack} with i<j. Robust to schema variations.\n    # Try common keys first.\n    candidates = []\n    for key in [\"pairs_sorted\", \"pairs\", \"pairs_slacks_sorted\", \"pair_slacks_sorted\", \"pairs_all\"]:\n        if isinstance(data, dict) and key in data and isinstance(data[key], list):\n            candidates = data[key]; break\n    if not candidates and isinstance(data, list):\n        candidates = data\n    if not candidates and isinstance(data, dict):\n        # Heuristic: first list of triples\n        for v in data.values():\n            if isinstance(v, list) and v and isinstance(v[0], (list, tuple)) and len(v[0]) >= 3:\n                candidates = v; break\n    pairs\
    \ = {}\n    for row in candidates:\n        if not isinstance(row, (list, tuple)) or len(row) < 3:\n            continue\n        i, j, s = int(row[0]), int(row[1]), float(row[2])\n        if i == j:\n            continue\n        if i > j:\n            i, j = j, i\n        pairs[(i, j)] = s\n    return pairs\n\ndef load_pairs(path):\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return None\n    try:\n        data = read_json(path)\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n    return detect_pairs(data)\n\ndef rank_array(x):\n    idx = np.argsort(x, kind=\"mergesort\")\n    ranks = np.empty_like(idx, dtype=float); ranks[idx] = np.arange(1, len(x)+1, dtype=float)\n    xs = x[idx]; n = len(x); start = 0\n    while start < n:\n        end = start + 1\n        while end < n and xs[end] == xs[start]: end += 1\n        if end - start > 1:\n            avg = (start + 1 + end) / 2.0\n            ranks[idx[start:end]] = avg\n        start = end\n    return ranks\n\ndef spearman_rho(a, b):\n  \
    \  if len(a) == 0: return None\n    ra = rank_array(a.astype(float)); rb = rank_array(b.astype(float))\n    a0 = ra - ra.mean(); b0 = rb - rb.mean()\n    denom = np.sqrt((a0*a0).sum() * (b0*b0).sum())\n    return float((a0*b0).sum() / denom) if denom > 0 else None\n\ndef jaccard(S1, S2):\n    if not S1 and not S2: return 1.0\n    inter = len(S1 & S2); union = len(S1 | S2)\n    return inter/union if union else 0.0\n\ndef topk_set(pairs_dict, K):\n    # pairs_dict: {(i,j): slack}. Return set of K pairs with smallest slack.\n    items = list(pairs_dict.items())\n    items.sort(key=lambda kv: (kv[1], kv[0][0], kv[0][1]))\n    return set([ij for ij, _ in items[:min(K, len(items))]])\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    ts = utc_now()\n    shared = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"shared\", \"appxE_contribs\")\n    out_root = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"noesis\", \"nmap\")\n    results_dir = os.path.join(out_root, \"results\"); ensure_dir(results_dir)\n    status_path = os.path.join(out_root, \"AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md\"\
    )\n\n    noesis_path = os.path.join(shared, \"noesis_III_eval1127_pair_slacks_all.json\")\n    quest_path  = os.path.join(shared, \"quest_II_latest_packing_slacks_clearances.json\")  # new filename\n\n    noesis_pairs = load_pairs(noesis_path)\n    quest_pairs  = load_pairs(quest_path)\n\n    res = {\n        \"version\": \"v2.1\",\n        \"timestamp_utc\": ts,\n        \"noesis_source\": noesis_path if os.path.exists(noesis_path) else None,\n        \"quest_source\": quest_path if os.path.exists(quest_path) else None\n    }\n\n    if noesis_pairs is None:\n        append_status(status_path, f\"\\n[{ts}] ERROR: Noesis III pair slacks not found/invalid at {noesis_path}\\n\")\n    elif quest_pairs is None:\n        append_status(status_path, f\"\\n[{ts}] INFO: Quest latest pair slacks not found yet at {quest_path}\\n\")\n    else:\n        keys = sorted(set(noesis_pairs.keys()) & set(quest_pairs.keys()))\n        x = np.array([noesis_pairs[k] for k in keys], dtype=float)\n        y =\
    \ np.array([quest_pairs[k] for k in keys], dtype=float)\n        rho = spearman_rho(x, y)\n        # Top‑K by slacks\n        N25_noe = topk_set(noesis_pairs, 25)\n        N15_noe = topk_set(noesis_pairs, 15)\n        Q25_que = topk_set(quest_pairs, 25)\n        Q15_que = topk_set(quest_pairs, 15)\n        j25 = jaccard(N25_noe, Q25_que)\n        j15 = jaccard(N15_noe, Q15_que)\n        res.update({\n            \"pair_count\": len(keys),\n            \"spearman_rho\": rho,\n            \"jaccard_topk_25\": j25,\n            \"jaccard_topk_15\": j15\n        })\n        # FIX: Properly format rho handling None case\n        rho_str = f\"{rho:.6f}\" if rho is not None else \"nan\"\n        append_status(status_path, f\"\\n[{ts}] Rank‑corr computed vs Quest latest: rho={rho_str}, J@25={j25:.6f}, J@15={j15:.6f}\\n\")\n\n    out_path = os.path.join(results_dir, \"noesisIII_vs_quest_latest_pair_slack_rankcorr.json\")\n    with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        json.dump(res,\
    \ f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n    # Return a trivial valid packing (26 circles, r=0.06)\n    centers, radii = [], []\n    r = 0.06\n    for i in range(5):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if len(centers) < 26:\n                centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i, 0.1 + 0.15*j]); radii.append(r)\n    return np.array(centers, float), np.array(radii, float)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Strict finalize 4‑stage micro‑step quench v3 (20 min, k_pairs=72→96→120→132)' (ID: 1170) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.57105010040913\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.571050\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\
