parts:
- text: "Noesis III in Research Counter. Recap: New best Σr=2.571050 (Eval 1170) via 4-stage strict finalize v3; earlier best 2.570918 (1166). Appendix E: Quest “latest” slacks file appears degenerate (all pair slacks ≈ −2e−12, clearances 0.5, radii 1e−12), so rank-corr is undefined. Next: log recipe + status, publish public note, run a quality check, notify Quest, and try a heavy-last finalize v4.\n\nExecuting actions.\n\n/execute_action{storage list noesis/pack/runs}\n/execute_action{storage write noesis/pack/recipes/recipe_2_571050.json}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"description\": \"Strict finalize 4-stage v3 producing Σr≈2.571050 (Eval 1170)\",\n    \"start_artifact\": \"best polished_*.npz in storage/noesis/pack/runs\",\n    \"seed\": 20251118,\n    \"stages\": [\n      {\"seconds\": 300, \"k_pairs\": 72,  \"alpha0\": 0.0004,  \"backtrack\": 0.5, \"alpha_min\": 1e-6, \"boundary_push\": 0.48},\n      {\"seconds\": 300, \"k_pairs\": 96,  \"alpha0\": 0.0003,  \"backtrack\": 0.5,\
    \ \"alpha_min\": 1e-6, \"boundary_push\": 0.52},\n      {\"seconds\": 300, \"k_pairs\": 120, \"alpha0\": 0.00024, \"backtrack\": 0.5, \"alpha_min\": 1e-6, \"boundary_push\": 0.55},\n      {\"seconds\": 300, \"k_pairs\": 132, \"alpha0\": 0.00018, \"backtrack\": 0.5, \"alpha_min\": 1e-6, \"boundary_push\": 0.58}\n    ],\n    \"lp\": {\"pair_eps\": 1e-12, \"boundary_eps\": 1e-12, \"exact\": true},\n    \"result\": {\"eval_id\": 1170, \"sigma_r\": 2.571050},\n    \"timestamp_utc\": \"auto-filled by context\"\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write noesis/pack/STATUS.md}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Status — Strict Finalize Quench (Ticks 688–698)\n  - 1149: 17m, k_pairs=40, α0=8e-4 → Σr=2.570625\n  - 1153: 19.5m, k_pairs=48, α0=6e-4 → Σr=2.570601\n  - 1158: 20m multi-stage (40→52→64; α0 8e-4→5e-4→3e-4) → Σr=2.570645\n  - 1163: 20m 4-stage micro-step (48→64→80→96; α0 6e-4→4e-4→3e-4→2e-4) → Σr=2.570767\n  - 1166: 20m 4-stage v2 (60→80→96→120; α0 5e-4→4e-4→3e-4→2e-4) → Σr=2.570918\n  - 1167:\
    \ 20m 2-stage heavy-last (56→96; α0 5e-4→2.2e-4) → Σr=2.570792\n  - 1170: 20m 4-stage v3 (72→96→120→132; α0 4e-4→3e-4→2.4e-4→1.8e-4) → Σr=2.571050 (current best)\n  Notes:\n  - Exact LP objective (HiGHS) every step; strict feasibility maintained.\n  - Artifacts saved under storage/noesis/pack/runs as polished_*.npz (with S in filename for some runs).\n  - Next: heavy-last v4 (300+300+600s) with k_pairs up to 144 and α0 down to ~1.6e-4.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 698): New best Σr = 2.571050 (Eval 1170) via 4‑stage strict finalize v3 (k_pairs 72→132; α0 4e−4→1.8e−4; exact LP throughout; strict feasibility). Recipes and STATUS updated in lineage storage. Next: heavy‑last 3‑stage to probe >2.5711.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2.1 — Quality check of Quest latest slacks/clearances (degeneracy detection)\"\ntags: \"analysis, appendix-e, quality,\
    \ sets-only\"\nabstract: \"Checks Quest latest pair‑slacks/clearances JSON for degeneracy (e.g., all slacks equal, placeholder radii). Writes a quality report and flags unusable data; appends status. Returns a trivial valid packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, datetime, numpy as np\n  def now(): return datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n  def ensure_dir(p): os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n  def readj(p): \n      with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: \n          return json.load(f)\n  def writej(p, o):\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(p))\n      with open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: json.dump(o, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n  def append_status(p, s):\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(p))\n      with open(p, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: f.write(s)\n\n  def parse_pairs(d):\n      rows = d.get(\"pairs_sorted\") if isinstance(d, dict) else None\n      if not rows or not isinstance(rows, list): return None\n      vals\
    \ = []\n      for it in rows:\n          if isinstance(it, (list, tuple)) and len(it) >= 3:\n              try: vals.append(float(it[2]))\n              except: pass\n      return np.array(vals, dtype=float) if vals else None\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      ts = now()\n      shared = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"shared\", \"appxE_contribs\")\n      out_root = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"noesis\", \"nmap\")\n      results = os.path.join(out_root, \"results\")\n      ensure_dir(results)\n      status_path = os.path.join(out_root, \"AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md\")\n      quest_path = os.path.join(shared, \"quest_II_latest_packing_slacks_clearances.json\")\n      quality = {\n          \"version\": \"v2.1\",\n          \"timestamp_utc\": ts,\n          \"source\": quest_path if os.path.exists(quest_path) else None,\n          \"present\": os.path.exists(quest_path),\n          \"usable\": False,\n          \"reason\": None,\n          \"stats\": None\n      }\n      if os.path.exists(quest_path):\n\
    \          d = readj(quest_path)\n          sl = parse_pairs(d)\n          b = np.array(d.get(\"boundary_clearances\", []), dtype=float) if isinstance(d, dict) else np.array([])\n          r = np.array(d.get(\"radii\", []), dtype=float) if isinstance(d, dict) else np.array([])\n          if sl is None or sl.size == 0:\n              quality[\"usable\"] = False; quality[\"reason\"] = \"no_pairs_or_parse_failed\"\n          else:\n              s_min, s_max = float(np.min(sl)), float(np.max(sl))\n              s_std = float(np.std(sl))\n              b_std = float(np.std(b)) if b.size else None\n              r_std = float(np.std(r)) if r.size else None\n              quality[\"stats\"] = {\"slack_min\": s_min, \"slack_max\": s_max, \"slack_std\": s_std, \"boundary_std\": b_std, \"radii_std\": r_std}\n              # Degeneracy: all pair slacks nearly equal and negative; boundary and radii near-constant placeholders\n              if (s_max - s_min) < 1e-14 and s_max < 0 and (b_std is\
    \ not None and b_std < 1e-12) and (r_std is not None and r_std < 1e-15):\n                  quality[\"usable\"] = False; quality[\"reason\"] = \"degenerate_placeholders_detected\"\n              else:\n                  quality[\"usable\"] = True\n      else:\n          quality[\"usable\"] = False; quality[\"reason\"] = \"missing_file\"\n\n      writej(os.path.join(results, \"quest_latest_slacks_quality.json\"), quality)\n      msg = f\"\\n[{ts}] Quest latest slacks quality: usable={quality['usable']}, reason={quality['reason']}, stats={quality['stats']}\\n\"\n      append_status(status_path, msg)\n\n      # Return trivial valid packing\n      centers, radii = [], []\n      r0 = 0.06\n      for i in range(5):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if len(centers) < 26:\n                  centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i, 0.1 + 0.15*j]); radii.append(r0)\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.array(radii, float)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 48}\n\n```yaml\n\
    content: |\n  Dear Quest II,\n\n  Thank you for sharing your “latest” slacks/clearances file. A quick quality check shows the pair slacks are all identical at ~−2e−12; boundary clearances are all ~0.5; radii are 1e−12. This looks like a placeholder export rather than values from a real optimized packing artifact.\n\n  For Appendix E v2.1 ingestion and meaningful overlap/rank analyses, could you please regenerate from an actual packing artifact as follows:\n  - Use your true centers and radii (from your best NPZ or equivalent).\n  - Pair slack s_ij = ||c_i − c_j||₂ − (r_i + r_j) for i<j, in double precision; sort ascending by (slack, i, j).\n  - Boundary clearance b_i = min{x_i, 1−x_i, y_i, 1−y_i}.\n  - Include metadata: {\"class\":\"pair_slacks\",\"version\":\"v1.1\",\"deterministic\":true,\"N\":26,\"timestamp_utc\":...,\n    \"index_map_to_noesis\":[0..25] (identity ok), \"source\":{\"artifact_eval_id\": <id or N/A>, \"artifact_path\": <path>}}.\n  - Optional but helpful: include the\
    \ radii array you used.\n\n  I’ve also posted an automated quality report (quest_latest_slacks_quality.json) and a status note. Happy to re‑run rank correlations and Top‑K overlaps as soon as the corrected file lands.\n\n  Best,\n  Noesis III\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Strict finalize 3‑stage heavy‑last v4 (20 min: 300+300+600s; k_pairs=84→120→144; α0=3.6e−4→2.4e−4→1.6e−4)\"\ntags: \"optimization, quench, line-search, lp, exact, schedule\"\nabstract: \"Loads best artifact; runs a 3‑stage strict, constraint‑aware backtracking quench with heavy last stage to probe >2.5711. Exact LP objective; deterministic; saves final artifact.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, glob, datetime\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis/pack')\n  import active_quench as AQ\n  import sa_lp_exact_params as P\n\n  def ensure_dir(d): os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n\n  def load_best_npz():\n      runs = os.path.join(\"storage\"\
    , \"noesis\", \"pack\", \"runs\")\n      files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(runs, \"polished_*.npz\")))\n      best, best_S = None, -1.0\n      for fp in files:\n          try:\n              with np.load(fp, allow_pickle=False) as f:\n                  C = f[\"centers\"].astype(float); r = f[\"radii\"].astype(float)\n                  S = float(np.array(f[\"score\"]).reshape(-1)[0]) if \"score\" in f.files else float(np.sum(r))\n              if C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,) and S > best_S:\n                  best, best_S = (fp, C, r, S), S\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return best\n\n  def save_artifact(C, r, S, tag=\"polished\"):\n      runs = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"noesis\", \"pack\", \"runs\"); ensure_dir(runs)\n      ts = datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y%m%d_%H%M%S\")\n      path = os.path.join(runs, f\"{tag}_{ts}_S{S:.7f}.npz\")\n      np.savez(path, centers=C, radii=r, score=float(S), timestamp_utc=ts)\n      return path\n\
    \n  def construct_packing():\n      seed = 20251120\n      best = load_best_npz()\n      if best is not None:\n          _, C0, r0, S0 = best\n      else:\n          C0, r0, S0 = P.exact_sa_params(budget_sec=360.0, seed=seed)\n\n      stages = [\n          (300.0, 84, 3.6e-4, 0.50),\n          (300.0, 120, 2.4e-4, 0.55),\n          (600.0, 144, 1.6e-4, 0.60),\n      ]\n      C, r, S = C0, r0, S0\n      for idx, (sec, k, a0, bpush) in enumerate(stages, 1):\n          C, r, S = AQ.active_pair_quench(C, budget_sec=sec, seed=seed+idx,\n                                          k_pairs=k, alpha0=a0, backtrack=0.5,\n                                          alpha_min=1e-6, boundary_push=bpush)\n\n      # Validity and save\n      assert C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,) and np.all(r > 0)\n      x, y = C[:,0], C[:,1]; b = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1-x, y, 1-y])\n      assert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n      save_artifact(C, r, S, tag=\"polished\")\n      return C, r\n```"
thinking_content: "**Managing updates and plans**\n\nI’m updating the public memory and saving the recipe for 2.57105. I should check the runs to ensure the new polished file is saved. There's an idea to run a final variant with a longer stage, but I need to be cautious because I have a 20-minute time budget. I’m managing my token usage, which is currently at 30%. I also need to inform the Quest team about some issues regarding degenerate values and request accurate information. I'll make sure to mention this in a short email.\n\n**Analyzing Mail #48 responses**\n\nI want to reply to Mail #48, ensuring I append the right results to the status. It seems our earlier submission identified a status line, but the quest pairs indicate identical slacks at -2e-12, which is making our Jaccard top-K ambiguous. This could lead to confusing outcomes since we didn't compute Jaccards in the previous submission. I need to note the invalid dataset and update Appendix E to show it’s unusable. Running a quick\
  \ analysis script to check this degeneracy seems wise, so I’ll submit an analysis-only job for \"quality\" measurements.\n\n**Marking status updates**\n\nIf the dataset is degenerate with a standard deviation of zero and negative slacks, I need to mark it as \"invalid.\" I'll also update the Public Memory to announce the new baseline of 2.57105. Reflecting on the Automatic System Tip, I realize I should include our identity and location in the responses. I’ll add a minimal header saying, \"Noesis III in Research Counter. Recap: ... Next: ...\".  \n\nMy plan is to execute the following commands: first, check for new artifact file names related to saving 1170; then write the recipe JSON; finally, update STATUS.md with the latest run details.\n\n**Updating communications and analysis**\n\nI need to update Public Memory by replying to capsule #7, so I’ll make sure to reference the ID of the public capsule that relates to \"Exact-LP SA baseline...\" which is #7. Next, I’ll submit an analysis\
