tick: 703
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{review 1185}\n/execute_action{storage list shared/appxE_contribs}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Appendix E v2.1 — Watcher: ingest Quest latest slacks/clearances (multi-name) and compute overlap vs NoesisIII Eval1127\"\ntags: \"analysis, appendix-e, rank-correlation, overlap, sets-only, watcher\"\nabstract: \"Scans shared/appxE_contribs for Quest’s corrected latest slacks/clearances under multiple filenames; aligns with Noesis III Eval1127 pair slacks; computes Spearman rank correlation and Top‑K Jaccards (K=25,15); writes results and status. Returns a trivial valid packing.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os, json, datetime, numpy as np\n\n  def utc_now(): return datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n  def ensure_dir(p): os.makedirs(p, exist_ok=True)\n  def read_json(p):\n      with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: return json.load(f)\n  def append_status(p, s):\n      ensure_dir(os.path.dirname(p))\n\
    \      with open(p, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: f.write(s)\n\n  def detect_pairs(data):\n      # Return dict {(i,j): slack} with i<j\n      candidates = []\n      if isinstance(data, dict):\n          for key in [\"pairs_sorted\", \"pairs\", \"pairs_slacks_sorted\", \"pair_slacks_sorted\", \"pairs_all\"]:\n              if key in data and isinstance(data[key], list):\n                  candidates = data[key]; break\n      if not candidates and isinstance(data, list):\n          candidates = data\n      if not candidates and isinstance(data, dict):\n          for v in data.values():\n              if isinstance(v, list) and v and isinstance(v[0], (list, tuple)) and len(v[0]) >= 3:\n                  candidates = v; break\n      pairs = {}\n      for row in candidates:\n          if not isinstance(row, (list, tuple)) or len(row) < 3: continue\n          i, j, s = int(row[0]), int(row[1]), float(row[2])\n          if i == j: continue\n          if i > j: i, j = j, i\n          pairs[(i,\
    \ j)] = s\n      return pairs\n\n  def load_pairs(path):\n      if not os.path.exists(path): return None\n      try: return detect_pairs(read_json(path))\n      except Exception: return None\n\n  def rank_array(x):\n      idx = np.argsort(x, kind=\"mergesort\")\n      ranks = np.empty_like(idx, dtype=float); ranks[idx] = np.arange(1, len(x)+1, dtype=float)\n      xs = x[idx]; n = len(x); a = 0\n      while a < n:\n          b = a + 1\n          while b < n and xs[b] == xs[a]: b += 1\n          if b - a > 1:\n              avg = (a + 1 + b) / 2.0\n              ranks[idx[a:b]] = avg\n          a = b\n      return ranks\n\n  def spearman_rho(a, b):\n      if len(a) == 0: return None\n      ra = rank_array(a.astype(float)); rb = rank_array(b.astype(float))\n      a0 = ra - ra.mean(); b0 = rb - rb.mean()\n      denom = np.sqrt((a0*a0).sum() * (b0*b0).sum())\n      return float((a0*b0).sum() / denom) if denom > 0 else None\n\n  def jaccard(S1, S2):\n      if not S1 and not S2: return 1.0\n\
    \      inter = len(S1 & S2); uni = len(S1 | S2)\n      return inter/uni if uni else 0.0\n\n  def topk_set(pairs_dict, K):\n      items = list(pairs_dict.items())\n      items.sort(key=lambda kv: (kv[1], kv[0][0], kv[0][1]))\n      return set([ij for ij, _ in items[:min(K, len(items))]])\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      ts = utc_now()\n      shared = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"shared\", \"appxE_contribs\")\n      out_root = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"noesis\", \"nmap\")\n      results_dir = os.path.join(out_root, \"results\"); ensure_dir(results_dir)\n      status_path = os.path.join(out_root, \"AGGREGATOR_v2_1_STATUS.md\")\n\n      # Noesis reference\n      noe_path = os.path.join(shared, \"noesis_III_eval1127_pair_slacks_all.json\")\n      noesis_pairs = load_pairs(noe_path)\n\n      # Quest candidates (multi-name support)\n      quest_candidates = [\n          os.path.join(shared, \"quest_II_latest_packing_slacks_clearances.json\"),\n          os.path.join(shared, \"quest_II_latest_slacks.json\"\
    ),\n          os.path.join(shared, \"latest_slacks.json\"),\n      ]\n      quest_path = next((p for p in quest_candidates if os.path.exists(p)), None)\n      quest_pairs = load_pairs(quest_path) if quest_path else None\n\n      res = {\n          \"version\": \"v2.1\",\n          \"timestamp_utc\": ts,\n          \"noesis_source\": noe_path if os.path.exists(noe_path) else None,\n          \"quest_source\": quest_path\n      }\n\n      if noesis_pairs is None:\n          append_status(status_path, f\"\\n[{ts}] ERROR: Noesis III pair slacks not found at {noe_path}\\n\")\n      elif quest_pairs is None:\n          append_status(status_path, f\"\\n[{ts}] INFO: Quest latest pair slacks not present yet under {quest_candidates}\\n\")\n      else:\n          keys = sorted(set(noesis_pairs.keys()) & set(quest_pairs.keys()))\n          x = np.array([noesis_pairs[k] for k in keys], dtype=float)\n          y = np.array([quest_pairs[k] for k in keys], dtype=float)\n          rho = spearman_rho(x,\
    \ y)\n          N25_noe = topk_set(noesis_pairs, 25); N15_noe = topk_set(noesis_pairs, 15)\n          Q25_que = topk_set(quest_pairs, 25); Q15_que = topk_set(quest_pairs, 15)\n          j25 = jaccard(N25_noe, Q25_que); j15 = jaccard(N15_noe, Q15_que)\n          res.update({\"pair_count\": len(keys), \"spearman_rho\": rho, \"jaccard_topk_25\": j25, \"jaccard_topk_15\": j15})\n          rho_str = f\"{rho:.6f}\" if rho is not None else \"nan\"\n          append_status(status_path, f\"\\n[{ts}] Rank‑corr vs Quest latest: rho={rho_str}, J@25={j25:.6f}, J@15={j15:.6f}\\n\")\n\n      out_path = os.path.join(results_dir, \"noesisIII_vs_quest_latest_pair_slack_rankcorr.json\")\n      with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n          json.dump(res, f, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2, sort_keys=True)\n\n      # Return a trivial valid packing\n      centers, radii = [], []\n      r = 0.06\n      for i in range(5):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if len(centers) < 26:\n  \
    \                centers.append([0.1 + 0.2*i, 0.1 + 0.15*j]); radii.append(r)\n      return np.array(centers, float), np.array(radii, float)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Maximizing Progress Steps**\n\nTo maximize progress, I should start by evaluating poll 1185 to check its score. If it's finished, I'll log the recipe, update the status, and post a PM update. I could explore a variant called \"micro-chill v8,\" making minor adjustments, but I need to avoid too many simultaneous evaluations. We can ingest Quest's corrected slacks when they are available and check for shared contributions. Lastly, I'm managing token usage effectively at 92k tokens, which is not critical. I'll ensure to provide conciseness in my comments.\n\n**Continuing with Actions**\n\nBased on the last outputs, I see that the agent scheduled v7 and documented the recipe and status. Next, I’ll need to execute a couple of actions: reviewing action 1185 and listing shared contributions. If there are new Quest files, I should run the aggregator for rank-corr and jaccard calculations. However, I need to be flexible with the filenames since they might provide variations.\
  \ I'll create a new ingestion submission to check for any of the accepted file names.\n\n**Planning for Efficiency**\n\nTo save tokens, I might just list the necessary elements and run the aggregator code if I see them. I need to propose a final schedule for \"v8,\" which will include a two-stage plan with larger k_pairs (increasing from 126 to 180) and a smaller alpha0 (from 2.4e-4 to 1.1e-4). \n\nI should also explore alternative strategies like symmetric pair stepping or block coordinate methods. The last micro-chill used a boundary_push of 0.57 to 0.63, and I might escalate it to 0.64, but I have to watch for diminishing returns. Additionally, I should keep the updates concise and refresh public memory after identifying the new best results.\n\n**Next Steps for Progress**\n\nRight now, there’s no new best above 2.571171 since v7 isn't finished. My next move is to review 1185, but if it’s still running, there's not much I can do. I’m considering implementing the aggregator as a separate\
  \ evaluation while using \"storage list\" to check for file presence.\n\nIt would be good to create a \"watcher\" aggregator that can parse the necessary file names, but that's extra code. The user probably expects ongoing lab actions, so my proposed steps are: review 1185, check for the presence of files in shared contributions, and then submit the aggregator. Even if files are missing, the aggregator should run smoothly based on earlier performance.\n\n**Planning Aggregator Actions**\n\nGiven the token limitations, I’ll submit an aggregator code that scans for multiple candidate filenames while keeping the code concise for evaluation compliance. It’s a good idea to review 1185 first, then list shared contributions, and finally submit the aggregator that handles file scanning and results writing.\n\nIf 1185 produces a new best, I’ll update the recipes and status. I’ll ensure that the aggregator can read candidate files, compute necessary correlations, and write results accordingly. Also,\
  \ I might propose a new finalizer to improve performance, but I won’t start more than two experiments concurrently. So, let's focus on these actions!"
