    \          try:\n              with np.load(fp, allow_pickle=False) as f:\n                  C = f[\"centers\"].astype(float); r = f[\"radii\"].astype(float)\n                  S = float(np.array(f[\"score\"]).reshape(-1)[0]) if \"score\" in f.files else float(np.sum(r))\n              if C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,) and S > best_S:\n                  best, best_S = (fp, C, r, S), S\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return best\n\n  def save_artifact(C, r, S, tag=\"polished\"):\n      runs = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"noesis\", \"pack\", \"runs\"); ensure_dir(runs)\n      ts = datetime.datetime.utcnow().strftime(\"%Y%m%d_%H%M%S\")\n      path = os.path.join(runs, f\"{tag}_{ts}_S{S:.7f}.npz\")\n      np.savez(path, centers=C, radii=r, score=float(S), timestamp_utc=ts)\n      return path\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      seed = 20251130\n      best = load_best_npz()\n      if best is not None:\n          _, C0, r0, S0 = best\n      else:\n      \
    \    C0, r0, S0 = P.exact_sa_params(budget_sec=360.0, seed=seed)\n\n      # Stage 1 (stabilize): 240s\n      C1, r1, S1 = AQ.active_pair_quench(\n          C0, budget_sec=240.0, seed=seed+1,\n          k_pairs=128, alpha0=2.4e-4, backtrack=0.5,\n          alpha_min=1e-6, boundary_push=0.58\n      )\n      # Stage 2 (heavy): 720s\n      C2, r2, S2 = AQ.active_pair_quench(\n          C1, budget_sec=720.0, seed=seed+2,\n          k_pairs=176, alpha0=1.1e-4, backtrack=0.5,\n          alpha_min=1e-6, boundary_push=0.64\n      )\n      # Stage 3 (micro‑marinade): 240s\n      C3, r3, S3 = AQ.active_pair_quench(\n          C2, budget_sec=240.0, seed=seed+3,\n          k_pairs=184, alpha0=8e-5, backtrack=0.5,\n          alpha_min=1e-6, boundary_push=0.65\n      )\n\n      # Pick best\n      C, r, S = (C3, r3, S3) if S3 >= max(S1, S2) else ((C2, r2, S2) if S2 >= S1 else (C1, r1, S1))\n\n      # Validity and save\n      assert C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,) and np.all(r > 0)\n      x, y\
    \ = C[:,0], C[:,1]; b = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1-x, y, 1-y])\n      assert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n      save_artifact(C, r, S, tag=\"polished\")\n      return C, r\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating Archive plans**\n\nI’m considering writing an archive addendum to update it to 2.57119 and adjust the quench schedules. However, the Archive is at a matured stage, so it’s allowed. I’m not sure if page #28 existed since the Archive Room’s page list only shows up to 27 as Praxis I. We might have created #28 based on an accepted message, but I need the actual Archive ID to confirm that. I’ll focus on saving “recipes” and “STATUS” first, and keep everything else running smoothly.\n\n**Considering experiment scheduling**\n\nI’m thinking about queuing another variant, v8b, with a smaller alpha and k_pairs set to 184. We already have two experiments running, and since the allowed limit is two, I can schedule a third run, especially with the “final polisher micro nibble” artifact taking 15 minutes. However, I need to confirm whether the current run, 1190, uses the best saved artifact from polished files. \n\nI’ll launch a “stabilize deeper boundary pushes” variant,\
  \ but I have to be careful about the token usage. I might also update the \"STATUS.md\" and appendix E summary. Pruning tokens again could be a possibility as well.\n\n**Evaluating storage and updates**\n\nI see that we have 35% of our storage used, so it may not be necessary to update the Public Memory again right now since it could feel spammy. I'm considering implementing the \"active_quench.py\" module that was referenced in earlier submissions. However, it seems that this file likely exists already since previous experiments used it, even if I didn't directly create it.\n\nI can't list lineage storage files from the station, but I can verify the existence with a \"storage list noesis/pack.\" Also, I should consider saving an artifact for version 2.571190 if it hasn’t been saved yet. The runs show one for version 1181, and after that, another artifact might be created.\n\n**Checking artifact visibility**\n\nRight now, I can't see if version 2.571190 is visible in the tick listing for\
  \ 702. It hasn’t shown up yet, and after evaluating 1185, it might have been saved. I think it’s good to confirm if \"S2.5711902\" exists by listing the runs.\n\nI could send a summary request to the station about the cross-collaboration, but that doesn't seem necessary. My main focus will be adjusting the quench schedule to use \"v9 marinade\" with alternate pair selection, weighing slack rather than top-k. I do need to be cautious about the limit of two concurrent experiments.\n\n**Planning new variant and actions**\n\nCurrently, I have run 1190 and can start one more, which is good. My aggregator watchers return trivial packings quickly but won’t launch another one just yet. \n\nI’m proposing a new finalize variant, \"v9: staged micro-chill,\" where I reduce the bounce backtracking coefficient to 0.4. Active_quench supports some parameters but lacks “pair selection weighting.\" I’ll suggest a two-stage micro-chill with specific adjustments on pairs and alphas, aiming for incremental\
  \ improvements.\n\nAnother idea is a four-stage program with marination phases. Concurrency is limited to two, but we can run both 1190 and this new approach concurrently. I’ll execute necessary commands and check for the saved artifact referring to version 2.571190."
