thinking_content: '**Considering token management and scheduling**


  I noticed the Archive Room listing isn''t showing because earlier pages detail a total of 27 across 3 pages. While I could check, it''s not urgent. I want to conserve tokens—I''ve used about 90k out of 270k, which is 33%—so I''ll keep messages concise. We can still finalize some schedule variations and consider unifying the plan. Maybe I''ll create a small "watcher" script to monitor quest data and trigger an aggregator.


  **Planning for memory notes and experiments**


  I can post a private memory note about our current best of 2.571331, with v17 running. The next steps might include considering alternate objectives or acceptance ratios, while looking at a "needle-move" finalization with a very small alpha tail. I might also adjust the v17 schedule to propose v18 with different k_pairs, but we can only submit one at a time since only 1207 is active. I want to avoid spamming with similarities while ensuring continuous experiments.


  **Managing public memory and submissions**


  I want to add to Public Memory, but that''s token-dependent. To clarify actions, I should use /execute_action commands with minimal commentary. I''m proposing to submit a v18 schedule variant with timings of 2m, 10m, 7.5m, and 0.5m while escalating k_pairs from 144 to 244 and lowering alpha to 2.2e-5. I''ll also note that we don''t need a new recipe since the best remains at 2.571331. I might update token management, prune further, and check on the "Public Memory Room." Then, it''s time to submit the new eval for v18!


  **Submitting v18 schedule**


  I''m considering join maturity, and we need to stick to rules about referencing other lineages, only reading existing storage. It’s allowed to read but not write to shared and noesis. I’ll propose the submission with the title "Strict finalize 4-stage micro-chill v18," detailing the schedule and parameters. I’ll import "active_quench" from storage to ensure it exists. We can submit with /execute_action{submit 1} and include YAML code for the v18 schedule. Let’s keep it straightforward and finalize the submission!


  **Managing concurrent experiments**


  I need to make sure we don''t exceed the limit of two experiments running at the same time. Since we currently have 1207 active, it means I can submit one more experiment now. That’s good! I’ll craft the code to be minimal, including the stage function and any other necessary components. It’s important to stay streamlined while making sure everything runs smoothly. Once I have that ready, I can return it for submission.'
