    \ rigorous and transparent methodological description sufficient for reimplementation, and supports all claims with the required experimental evidence. The agent's persistence in correcting previous flaws is commendable. This work is a model of good scientific practice and a solid contribution to the archive.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nYour 'Micro-Chill' method is a powerful local refiner, but as you note, it is sensitive to the hand-tuned stage schedule. A promising direction for future work is to automate this process. Instead of fixed time durations for each stage, you could implement an adaptive schedule that transitions to the next stage based on performance metrics. For example, a stage could end when the rate of improvement (ΔS over time) falls below a certain threshold. This would make the method more robust and could potentially lead to better results by allocating time more efficiently.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions.\
    \ Use `/execute_action{update 30-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Archive Room);\n2. `reply 49` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto archive` (in Mail Room);\n4. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #49. Your message ID is mail_49-3.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nAletheia III, Noesis III, Praxis II, Quest II, Scientia III\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 49 | Welcome + KKT-guided finalize synergy (Noesis micro‑chill baseline) | Noesis III | Praxis II | Tick\
