- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write noesis/pack/active_quench_adaptive.py}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np, time, math, glob, os\n  from sa_lp_exact_params import solve_radii_lp, hex_centers_26, clamp01\n  import active_quench as AQ\n\n  def pair_slacks(centers, r):\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n      D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1))\n      return D - (r[:, None] + r[None, :])\n\n  def topk_slack_mean(centers):\n      r, S, _ = solve_radii_lp(centers)\n      sl = pair_slacks(centers, r)\n      n = sl.shape[0]\n      vals = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i+1, n):\n              vals.append(float(sl[i, j]))\n      vals.sort()\n      K = min(128, len(vals))\n      return float(np.mean(vals[:K])), r, S\n\n  def find_best_npz(runs_dir):\n      files = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(runs_dir, \"polished_*.npz\")))\n      best = None; best_S = -1.0\n      for fp in files:\n          try:\n   \
    \           with np.load(fp, allow_pickle=False) as f:\n                  C = f[\"centers\"].astype(float)\n                  r = f[\"radii\"].astype(float)\n                  S = float(np.array(f[\"score\"]).reshape(-1)[0]) if \"score\" in f.files else float(np.sum(r))\n              if C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,) and S > best_S:\n                  best = (fp, C, r, S); best_S = S\n          except Exception:\n              continue\n      return best\n\n  class EMA:\n      def __init__(self, alpha):\n          self.alpha = float(alpha)\n          self.val = None\n      def update(self, x):\n          x = float(x)\n          if self.val is None:\n              self.val = x\n          else:\n              self.val = self.alpha * x + (1 - self.alpha) * self.val\n          return self.val\n\n  def adaptive_finalize(total_sec=1200.0, seed=20251205, segment_sec=30.0,\n                        eta_S=5e-6, eta_slack=1e-7, gamma_alpha=0.6, dK=12,\n                        k_pairs_init=176,\
    \ alpha0_init=1.2e-4, boundary_push_init=0.64,\n                        boundary_push_min=0.58):\n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      # Start from best artifact if available; else hex grid\n      runs_dir = os.path.join(\"storage\", \"noesis\", \"pack\", \"runs\")\n      best = find_best_npz(runs_dir)\n      if best is not None:\n          _, centers, r, S = best\n      else:\n          centers = clamp01(hex_centers_26())\n          r, S, _ = solve_radii_lp(centers)\n\n      # Initial metrics\n      slack_mean, r, S = topk_slack_mean(centers)\n\n      # EMAs over segment rates (Δ per second)\n      # segment-based EMA alpha ~ 1 - exp(-seg/τ); with τ≈10s → alpha≈1 - exp(-3) if seg=30s ≈ 0.95\n      ema_S = EMA(alpha=0.95)\n      ema_slack = EMA(alpha=0.95)\n\n      k_pairs = int(k_pairs_init)\n      alpha0 = float(alpha0_init)\n      boundary_push = float(boundary_push_init)\n\n      end_time = time.time() + float(total_sec)\n      seg_id = 0\n      while time.time() < end_time:\n\
    \          seg_budget = min(segment_sec, max(0.0, end_time - time.time()))\n          if seg_budget <= 0.0:\n              break\n          # Pre-segment state\n          S0 = S\n          slack0 = slack_mean\n\n          # Run one strict quench segment\n          centers, r, S = AQ.active_pair_quench(\n              centers, budget_sec=float(seg_budget), seed=int(seed + 1 + seg_id),\n              k_pairs=int(k_pairs), alpha0=float(alpha0),\n              backtrack=0.5, alpha_min=1e-6, boundary_push=float(boundary_push)\n          )\n          # Post-segment metrics (recompute slack frontier)\n          slack_mean, r, S = topk_slack_mean(centers)\n\n          # Rates\n          dS = S - S0\n          dSlack = slack0 - slack_mean  # reduction in mean(top-128) slack\n          rate_S = dS / max(1e-9, seg_budget)\n          rate_slack = dSlack / max(1e-9, seg_budget)\n\n          rS = ema_S.update(rate_S)\n          rSL = ema_slack.update(rate_slack)\n\n          # Transition logic (deterministic\
    \ thresholds)\n          plateau = (rS < eta_S) or (rSL < eta_slack)\n          if plateau:\n              alpha0 = max(alpha0 * float(gamma_alpha), 1e-6)\n              k_pairs = int(min(288, k_pairs + int(dK)))\n              if rSL < eta_slack and boundary_push > boundary_push_min:\n                  boundary_push = max(boundary_push_min, boundary_push * 0.95)\n\n          seg_id += 1\n\n      return centers, r, S\n```\n\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adaptive strict finalize v0 — EMA-based stage transitions (20 min)\"\ntags: \"optimization, finalize, lp, exact, adaptive, schedule\"\nabstract: \"Implements a deterministic adaptive strict-finalize controller: 30s segments with EMA of improvement rate (ΔΣr/time) and frontier reduction (mean of top-128 pair slack). When rates fall below thresholds, reduce step α0 and increase k_pairs. Starts from best saved artifact if available. Exact LP objective.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis/pack')\n\
    \  import active_quench_adaptive as AD\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      C, r, S = AD.adaptive_finalize(\n          total_sec=1200.0,\n          seed=20251205,\n          segment_sec=30.0,\n          eta_S=5e-6,\n          eta_slack=1e-7,\n          gamma_alpha=0.6,\n          dK=12,\n          k_pairs_init=176,\n          alpha0_init=1.2e-4,\n          boundary_push_init=0.64,\n          boundary_push_min=0.58\n      )\n      # Validity checks\n      assert C.shape == (26,2)\n      assert r.shape == (26,)\n      assert np.all(r > 0)\n      x, y = C[:,0], C[:,1]\n      b = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1-x, y, 1-y])\n      assert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n      return C, r\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating adaptive control methods**\n\nThe adaptive controller could potentially run the same function, but it might also require a quench for the entire budget. To adapt within the budget, I think we need smaller segments repeated with different parameters. Running stage segments of Δt_eval or chunk lengths could simulate inner steps. The active_pair_quench might return improved centers based on the budget, allowing repeated adjustments to α0, k_pairs, and boundary_push across calls. I’ll implement an \"adaptive_finalize\" to loop segments of 20 or 30 seconds until reaching the total budget.\n\n**Improving adaptive methods**\n\nI’m thinking we can adapt to focus on the S improvement rate and slack frontier changes computed through pair slacks at centers. I’ll calculate the mean of the top-K smallest slacks from the pair slacks function. \nMy plan is to write a script in noesis/pack/active_quench_adaptive.py that will include functions like pair_slacks, top_k_slack_mean,\
  \ and run_segment. I’ll call AQ.active_pair_quench with the specified parameters and budget segment, recording S to track improvements. Setting default thresholds will help guide the computations, including determining boundary productivity with minimal improvements.\n\n**Streamlining adaptive implementation**\n\nI think it might be simpler to implement base triggers with r_S and r_slack. I need to ensure that we use the exact LP solve to compute S, so I’ll call the \"solve_radii_lp\" function from sa_lp_exact_params, which is available. I plan to create a function called adaptive_finalize that takes parameters like budget_sec, seed, ema_tau, and segment_sec. I will compute results within a loop and submit a new evaluation using the best artifact. I'll also update public memory, noting that \"Adaptive finalize v0 submitted\" and maintain Appendix E from the previous export for eval1219.\n\n**Planning submission structure**\n\nI can run the aggregator to compute overlaps versus the latest\
  \ quest, but we've already set up an aggregator earlier for that purpose. While I could document this, it's not necessary right now; I want to focus on minimizing tokens. I’ll include just the essential code skeleton for submission. The submission requires the run.py code that includes the construct_packing function. I plan to import the new module from storage/noesis/pack and make sure to add 'sys.path.append('storage/noesis/pack')'. I’ll create the \"active_quench_adaptive.py\" file and outline the actions needed, including setting up the new evaluation with a focus on adaptive_finalize and necessary precautions about loading artifacts from storage.\n\n**Crafting the adaptive finalize code**\n\nI’ll set it up to use 300 seconds for adaptive finalize with the remaining budget, and for earlier budgets, I'll refine from the best C. Validity checks and accurate parameter values for thresholds will be a must. For twenty minutes (1200 seconds) with a 30-second segment, I need to hard-code\
  \ the thresholds and implement a top K of 128 for slack means. \n\nThe goal is to ensure the code is minimal while including necessary functions. I'll calculate pair slacks derived from radii, using results from solve_radii_lp, and address boundary push slowly as I loop through segments. Finally, I'll submit the run and optionally write a recipe file after evaluation, but I’ll keep commentary light to save tokens."
