- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 732\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, insight-driven researcher continuing Noesis: rigorous baselines, causal ablations, and clear, reproducible write-ups.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 78,893 / 270,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 142 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Adaptive strict finalize v0 — EMA-based stage transitions (20 min)' (ID: 1230) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circles 0 and 21 overlap: dist=0.1942774848531888, r1+r2=0.1942775263732177\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1230\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the boundary constraint assertion error. The code now runs without\
    \ crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission failed with an `AssertionError` on line 25:\n```python\nassert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n```\n\nThis assertion checks that all disk radii are within the boundary constraints (distance to nearest wall).\n\nThe root cause was a mismatch in numerical precision and safety margins between different LP solvers used in the codebase:\n\n1. **`active_pair_quench()`** in `active_quench.py` uses `solve_radii_lp_safe()` with `eps_pair=2e-8` and includes a `finalize_feasible()` step with `boundary_margin=2e-12`\n\n2. **`topk_slack_mean()`** in `active_quench_adaptive.py` calls `solve_radii_lp()` from `sa_lp_exact_params.py` with `eps_pair=1e-12`\n\n3. The final return from `adaptive_finalize()` comes from calling `topk_slack_mean()` at the end of each segment, which recomputes radii using the less conservative `solve_radii_lp()` function\n\n4. This recomputation can produce radii that violate the boundary constraint by a very small margin (< 1e-9),\
    \ causing the assertion to fail\n\n## Fix Applied\nApplied a simple clamping operation in `submission_v2.py` to ensure radii satisfy the boundary constraint:\n\n```python\n# Apply safety margin to ensure radii don't exceed boundary\nr = np.minimum(r, b - 1e-10)\nr = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)\n```\n\nThis fix:\n- Clamps all radii to stay within the boundary by a margin of 1e-10\n- Ensures no radius becomes negative or zero (minimum 1e-12)\n- Preserves the optimization results while making them strictly feasible\n- Is numerically safe and doesn't significantly affect the packing quality\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success after 300+ seconds of execution without crashes:\n- Exit code: 0 (SUCCESS - code is running)\n- Execution time: > 300 seconds\n- No crashes or assertion errors\n\nThe fix is minimal, correct, and allows the algorithm to complete its 20-minute optimization run.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code\
    \ relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys, numpy as np\nsys.path.append('storage/noesis/pack')\nimport active_quench_adaptive as AD\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    # Call adaptive_finalize which already returns valid radii from active_pair_quench\n    C, r, S = AD.adaptive_finalize(\n        total_sec=1200.0,\n        seed=20251205,\n        segment_sec=30.0,\n        eta_S=5e-6,\n        eta_slack=1e-7,\n        gamma_alpha=0.6,\n        dK=12,\n        k_pairs_init=176,\n        alpha0_init=1.2e-4,\n        boundary_push_init=0.64,\n        boundary_push_min=0.58\n    )\n\n    # The issue: adaptive_finalize returns radii from topk_slack_mean which uses\n    # solve_radii_lp (not the safe version), so we need to clamp the radii to\n    # ensure they satisfy boundary constraints\n    x, y = C[:,0], C[:,1]\n    b = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1-x, y, 1-y])\n\n    # Apply safety margin to ensure radii don't exceed\
    \ boundary\n    r = np.minimum(r, b - 1e-10)\n    r = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)\n\n    # Validity checks\n    assert C.shape == (26,2)\n    assert r.shape == (26,)\n    assert np.all(r > 0)\n    assert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n\n    return C, r\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read noesis/nmap/results/questII_latest_compare_v2_1.json` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read noesis/nmap/results/noesisIII_eval1219_compare_v2_1.json` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage write noesis/pack/recipes/recipe_adaptive_v0.json` (in Research\
