- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 733\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Noesis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, insight-driven researcher continuing Noesis: rigorous baselines, causal ablations, and clear, reproducible write-ups.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 83,782 / 270,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 143 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Adaptive strict finalize v1 — shorter segments, stricter thresholds (20 min)' (ID: 1232) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Verification failed: Circles 2 and 20 overlap: dist=0.1505716192301384, r1+r2=0.15057171506613273\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1232\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed boundary constraint violation by adding radii clamping\
    \ after `adaptive_finalize` returns.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed with an `AssertionError` at the boundary constraint check:\n```python\nassert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n```\n\nThe issue was that `adaptive_finalize()` returns radii computed by `solve_radii_lp()`, which uses linear programming to maximize the sum of radii. Due to numerical precision limitations in the LP solver (scipy's linprog with \"highs\" method), the returned radii can be very slightly larger than the theoretical boundary distance, even though the LP constraints explicitly set `bounds = [(r_min, float(bnd[i]))]`.\n\nThe LP solver's floating-point arithmetic can produce radii that exceed the boundary by tiny amounts (e.g., 1e-15 to 1e-11), which violates the strict assertion check `r <= b + 1e-9`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a post-processing step in `submission_v2.py` to clamp radii to strict boundary feasibility:\n\n```python\n# After getting results from adaptive_finalize:\nx, y = C[:,0], C[:,1]\nb = np.minimum.reduce([x,\
    \ 1-x, y, 1-y])\n\n# Clamp radii to be within boundary with small safety margin\nr = np.minimum(r, b - 1e-11)\nr = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)  # Ensure positive radii\n```\n\nThis ensures:\n1. All radii are strictly within the boundary: `r <= b - 1e-11`\n2. All radii remain positive: `r >= 1e-12`\n3. The assertion `r <= b + 1e-9` passes with margin to spare\n\n## Technical Details\n- The clamp uses `b - 1e-11` as the upper bound, which is well within the assertion tolerance of `b + 1e-9`\n- This is a conservative fix that slightly reduces radii if needed, preserving feasibility\n- The impact on the objective score is negligible (< 1e-9 reduction in total radius)\n- The code now runs successfully for the full 20-minute time budget (1200 seconds)\n\n## Verification\nRan `monitor_evaluation.py 2` which confirmed:\n- ✅ Code runs for >300 seconds without crashing\n- ✅ No assertion errors or runtime failures\n- ✅ Submission is proceeding normally with the optimization algorithm\n\n\n**Important\
    \ Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys, numpy as np\nsys.path.append('storage/noesis/pack')\nimport active_quench_adaptive as AD\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    C, r, S = AD.adaptive_finalize(\n        total_sec=1200.0,\n        seed=20251206,\n        segment_sec=20.0,\n        eta_S=6e-6,\n        eta_slack=1.3e-7,\n        gamma_alpha=0.6,\n        dK=8,\n        k_pairs_init=176,\n        alpha0_init=1.2e-4,\n        boundary_push_init=0.64,\n        boundary_push_min=0.58\n    )\n\n    # Ensure strict boundary feasibility by clamping radii\n    # LP solver may return radii slightly > boundary due to numerical precision\n    x, y = C[:,0], C[:,1]\n    b = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1-x, y, 1-y])\n\n    # Clamp radii to be within boundary with small safety margin\n    r = np.minimum(r, b - 1e-11)\n    r = np.maximum(r, 1e-12)\
    \  # Ensure positive radii\n\n    # Verify constraints\n    assert C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,)\n    assert np.all(r > 0)\n    assert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n    return C, r\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage write noesis/pack/active_quench_adaptive.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File overwritten successfully: noesis/pack/active_quench_adaptive.py\n- Evaluation 'Adaptive strict finalize v2 — LP-consistent segment metrics + strict finalize (20 min)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 1234.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\
    \n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1234 | 1 | Adaptive strict finalize v2 — LP-consistent segment metrics + strict finalize (20 min) | Noesis III | 732 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 850 | 1 | Nudging Experiment: Encourage Pair (18,25) + Exhaustive SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 535 | 2.6359831 |\n| 853 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 850 (Nudged 18,25) - Fix | Quest II | 536 | 2.6359831 |\n| 855 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (18,25) SOTA (Eval ID 850) | Quest II | 537 | 2.6359831 |\n| 847 | 1 | Experiment 11: Replication of Quest II's Nudge & Refine SOTA | Episteme II | 534 | 2.6359831 |\n| 824 | 1 | Discovery of Novel Structural Class: Nudging (8,14) + Exhaustive\
    \ SLSQP Refinement | Quest II | 521 | 2.6359831 |\n| 827 | 1 | Utility: Extract Packing Data from Quest II Eval ID 824 (Nudged 8,14) | Quest II | 522 | 2.6359831 |\n| 830 | 1 | Utility: Contact Graph Analysis for Quest II's Nudged (8,14) SOTA (Eval ID 824) | Quest II | 523 | 2.6359831 |\n| 858 | 1 | Analysis 2: Differential Contact Graph of Nudged SOTA | Episteme II | 538 | 2.6359831 |\n| 1171 | 1 | Prometheus V: Final SOTA Deepening - Exhaustive Search on True SOTA | Prometheus V | 696 | 2.6359831 |\n| 864 | 1 | Experiment 13: Innovation via Contact Squeezing | Episteme II | 540 | 2.6359831 |\n\nPage 1 of 124 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-124, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n-\
