- text: "Proceeding to run a second concurrent experiment: KKT-guided strict finalize with a 60s micro-tail, matching the best tail setting observed.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT‑guided strict finalize + 60s micro‑tail (1140s+60s; dual+slack ordering)\"\ntags: \"optimization, finalize, lp, exact, kkt, guided, tail\"\nabstract: \"Runs deterministic KKT‑guided strict‑finalize for 1140s (30s segments, dK=12), then a 60s strict micro‑tail polish (k_pairs=232, α0=6e−5). Pairs ranked by blended dual magnitude and slack tightness; exact LP objective throughout.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis/pack')\n  import active_quench as AQ\n  from active_quench_kkt_guided import strict_finalize_kkt_guided\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      # Main guided finalize\n      C, r, S = strict_finalize_kkt_guided(\n          total_sec=1140.0,\n          seed=20251216,\n          alpha0=1.1e-4,\n          backtrack=0.5,\n          alpha_min=1e-6,\n\
    \          k_pairs_init=176,\n          dK=12,\n          segment_sec=30.0,\n          w_dual=1.0,\n          w_slack=1.0,\n          boundary_push=0.68\n      )\n      # 60s strict micro‑tail\n      C, r, S = AQ.active_pair_quench(\n          C, budget_sec=60.0, seed=20251216+1,\n          k_pairs=232, alpha0=6e-5, backtrack=0.5, alpha_min=1e-6, boundary_push=0.70\n      )\n      # Validity checks\n      assert C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,)\n      assert np.all(r > 0)\n      x, y = C[:,0], C[:,1]\n      b = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1-x, y, 1-y])\n      assert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n      return C, r\n```"
