    \ best adaptive+tail).\n  - v1 + 60s tail, safe eps=1e−7 (1272): running.\n  Plan: run v1 + 120s tail (1080s + 120s) to check if KKT-guided benefits from a longer tail; then sweep (w_dual, w_slack) grid.\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT‑guided strict finalize v1 + 120s tail (1080s+120s; eps=5e−8)\"\ntags: \"optimization, finalize, lp, exact, kkt, guided\"\nabstract: \"Deterministic KKT‑guided strict‑finalize for 1080s (30s segments, dK=12) with strict projector (pair/boundary eps=5e−8), followed by a 120s micro‑tail. Dual+slack frontier ordering; exact LP objective throughout.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis/pack')\n  import active_quench as AQ\n  from active_quench_kkt_guided import strict_finalize_kkt_guided\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      C, r, S = strict_finalize_kkt_guided(\n          total_sec=1080.0,\n          seed=20251219,\n          alpha0=1.1e-4,\n          backtrack=0.5,\n          alpha_min=1e-6,\n\
    \          k_pairs_init=176,\n          dK=12,\n          segment_sec=30.0,\n          w_dual=1.0,\n          w_slack=1.0,\n          boundary_push=0.68,\n          pair_eps=5e-8,\n          boundary_eps=5e-8\n      )\n      C, r, S = AQ.active_pair_quench(\n          C, budget_sec=120.0, seed=20251219+1,\n          k_pairs=248, alpha0=5.5e-5, backtrack=0.5, alpha_min=1e-6, boundary_push=0.70\n      )\n      assert C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,)\n      assert np.all(r > 0)\n      x, y = C[:,0], C[:,1]\n      b = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1-x, y, 1-y])\n      assert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n      return C, r\n```"
