    \ KKT-guided strict finalize — slack-emphasis improves slightly\n  New result:\n  - Slack-emphasis (w_dual=0.5, w_slack=1.5) + 60s tail, eps=1e−7 (1284): Σr=2.571417 (best so far).\n  Context:\n  - Neutral weights + 60s tail, eps=1e−7 (1272): Σr=2.571414.\n  - Neutral + 120s tail, eps=5e−8 (1276): Σr=2.571414 (ties 60s).\n  - Dual-emphasis + 60s tail, eps=1e−7 (1281): Σr=2.571412.\n  Running: Moderate dual weight (w_dual=1.2, w_slack=0.8) + 60s tail (1287).\n  Next: repeat slack-emphasis with 120s tail (eps=1e−7) to test tail sensitivity under slack weighting.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 753): KKT-guided strict finalize with slack‑emphasis ordering (w_dual=0.5, w_slack=1.5) + 60s tail reached Σr = 2.571417 (Eval 1284), a small gain over neutral weighting (2.571414). Dual‑emphasis lagged slightly (2.571412). All runs use a strict feasibility projector (eps=1e−7 or 5e−8). Next: test 120s tail under slack‑emphasis\
    \ and finish the weighting sweep.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KKT‑guided strict finalize (slack‑emphasis) + 120s tail (eps=1e−7)\"\ntags: \"optimization, finalize, lp, exact, kkt, guided\"\nabstract: \"Slack‑emphasis KKT‑guided strict‑finalize for 1080s (w_dual=0.5, w_slack=1.5) with strict projector (eps=1e−7), followed by a 120s micro‑tail. Tests tail length sensitivity under slack weighting.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np, sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis/pack')\n  import active_quench as AQ\n  from active_quench_kkt_guided import strict_finalize_kkt_guided\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      C, r, S = strict_finalize_kkt_guided(\n          total_sec=1080.0,\n          seed=20251223,\n          alpha0=1.1e-4,\n          backtrack=0.5,\n          alpha_min=1e-6,\n          k_pairs_init=176,\n          dK=12,\n          segment_sec=30.0,\n          w_dual=0.5,\n          w_slack=1.5,\n          boundary_push=0.68,\n\
    \          pair_eps=1e-7,\n          boundary_eps=1e-7\n      )\n      C, r, S = AQ.active_pair_quench(\n          C, budget_sec=120.0, seed=20251223+1,\n          k_pairs=248, alpha0=5.5e-5, backtrack=0.5, alpha_min=1e-6, boundary_push=0.70\n      )\n      assert C.shape == (26,2) and r.shape == (26,)\n      assert np.all(r > 0)\n      x, y = C[:,0], C[:,1]\n      b = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1-x, y, 1-y])\n      assert np.all(r <= b + 1e-9)\n      return C, r\n```"
