- text: "Identity: Noesis III. Location: Archive Room.\nBrief recap: Over the last dozen ticks, I stabilized KKT-guided strict finalize with a strict feasibility projector, ran a weighting sweep (neutral, dual-emphasis, slack-emphasis) and tail-length ablations. Best so far: slack-emphasis + 60s tail at Σr = 2.571417 (Eval 1284). I exported Appendix E v2.1 artifacts for Eval 1284 and added an archive addendum summarizing the KKT-guided gains.\n\nReflection: The KKT-guided variant offers small but consistent improvements when it prioritizes frontier slacks more heavily than dual magnitudes. The strict projector (eps ~ 1e-7) has proven valuable for eliminating rare verification failures with negligible score impact. Tail length shows diminishing returns beyond 60s under KKT-guided ordering, unlike the earlier adaptive schedules where 120s occasionally helped. Next, I will standardize on the slack-emphasis + 60s tail recipe, finish the two-stage tail evaluation, then freeze and export final\
    \ Appendix E slices for the best artifact. To preserve headroom, I’ll prune the recent, verbose logs with concise, information-complete summaries.\n\nExecuting pruning to conserve tokens.\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"729-730\"\n    summary: |\n      Planning + Adaptive Finalize v0.\n      - 729: Wrote private plan (adaptive strict finalize + KKT-guided ablations); reviewed Token Management.\n      - 730: Implemented active_quench_adaptive.py (EMA-based stage controller) and submitted adaptive strict finalize v0 (20 min). Set up for feasibility fixes (strict projector) and follow-on comparisons.\n\n  - ticks: \"742-744\"\n    summary: |\n      Tail-length sweep consolidation and public update.\n      - 742: Logged recipe for 60s tail (Eval 1250 = 2.571412) and status; submitted 120s tail (1256, running).\n      - 743: 120s tail result (1256) = 2.571413 (≈ties 60s); saved recipe; public note summarizing\
    \ tail-length findings and preferred 60s setting.\n      - 744: Export plan for best artifact; queued KKT-guided weight sweep.\n\n  - ticks: \"746-755\"\n    summary: |\n      KKT-guided strict finalize: feasibility fix, weighting sweep, Appendix E updates, archive addendum.\n      - 746–747: KKT-guided v0 failed (overlap); added strict feasibility projector (pair/boundary eps=5e−8→1e−7). v1 (1269) = 2.571412; KKT-guided + 60s tail (1265) = 2.571413.\n      - 748–751: Safe eps=1e−7 + 60s tail (1272) = 2.571414; 120s tail (1276) = 2.571414; dual-emphasis (1281) = 2.571412; slack-emphasis (1284) = 2.571417 (best); moderate dual (1287) = 2.571412.\n      - 752–755: Exported Appendix E for Eval 1284 (Top‑K + pair slacks; overlaps vs 922/1127/1219/1256); submitted slack‑emphasis + 120s tail (1291) = 2.571414; submitted two‑stage 60s tail; wrote recipes; posted archive addendum summarizing KKT-guided gains and recommendations.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Organizing updates efficiently**\n\nI'm considering posting a public memory update about the KKT-guided slack-emphasis results. We've already shared one at tick 753, so I don't want to overload the public memory. The Automatic System Tips suggest keeping our messages concise and objective, so avoiding more posts makes sense. \n\nFor the Appendix E ingestion, I'll confirm that 1284 is the best option to move forward with and ensure everything is tracked effectively while keeping an eye on evaluations. My main focus should be on performing the prune action and crafting a thorough but concise summary of results and takeaways.\n\n**Compiling a concise summary**\n\nI'm looking to compile a summary of the recent evaluations and activities. \n\nFor 742, I noted a tail sweep with a 90s tail evaluation yielding 2.571392 and a 120s tail evaluation at 2.571413. I also wrote the recipes' status and posted a public update. \n\nThen for 743, I logged the recipe for the 120s tail,\
  \ updated the status, and shared a public note, with stable results. Next steps involve the KKT-guided weight sweep.\n\n**Consolidating evaluations**\n\nI noticed that the summary for 743 overlaps with 742, so I can incorporate it into a broader summary covering 742-744. \n\nMoving to 744, I exported for eval1256 and made a note to prune the earlier response. The logs show I created a recipe for KKT-guided tail120 and posted an update, which is good.\n\nFor 746, I created the KKT-guided file and submitted version 0, noting overlaps with 1263. Later steps involved submission of different versions, with scores and results being tracked, including the dual emphasis work and final submissions.\n\n**Summarizing evaluation results**\n\nAt 754, I recorded a moderate dual result of 2.571412 and submitted the slack emphasis 120s tail. Now for 755, I completed the Appendix E export for 1284, noted that the slack emphasis 120s tail resulted in 2.571414, and submitted a two-stage tail. I also posted\
  \ an archive addendum with KKT-guided results.\n\nI can create a comprehensive summary for 746-755 and consider pruning 729-730, which hasn’t been done yet. In that block, I'll recall the token management help and summarize the adaptive finalize code submission.\n\n**Finalizing summaries for pruning**\n\nFirst, I'll check earlier content to ensure I have everything right. At 729, we were focused on token management, and at 730, we wrote and submitted the active_quench_adaptive code. Since the system has noted, \"Pruned Ticks 731-734,\" it suggests that 730 included the adaptive finalize code.\n\nFor pruning, I can summarize 729-730 as: \"Post-Accept Plan in Private Memory, moved to token management help; wrote active_quench_adaptive v0, submitted adaptive finalize.\" I’ll also compile summaries for 742-744 and 746-755. I’ll make sure all blocks are consecutive and include proper reflection before executing the token management prune actions."
